window.ANALYSIS_DATA = {"plan": {"filename": "exp_analysis_planning_final_cohort.json", "url": "output/exp_analysis_planning_final_cohort.json", "text": "[\n  {\n    \"analysis_method\": \"Data import\",\n    \"operation\": \"Open \\\"D:/mimic-iv-3.1/hosp.duckdb\\\" read-only (DuckDB ATTACH ... READ_ONLY), copy the table final_cohort_patient_level unchanged with SELECT * to Parquet, and write nothing to the DuckDB file.\",\n    \"data_input\": {\"name\": \"hosp.duckdb::final_cohort_patient_level\", \"format\": \"DuckDB table\"},\n    \"data_output\": {\"name\": \"cohort_imported.parquet\", \"format\": \"Parquet\"}\n  },\n  {\n    \"analysis_method\": \"Schema and identifier validation\",\n    \"operation\": \"Verify 9902 rows and 146 columns, that subject_id and stay_id are nonmissing and unique (first qualifying septic ICU stay per patient) and that hadm_id is nonmissing. Write one row per column (dtype, missing count) and per identifier check, and stop if an identifier check fails.\",\n    \"data_input\": {\"name\": \"cohort_imported.parquet\", \"format\": \"Parquet\"},\n    \"data_output\": {\"name\": \"schema_validation.csv\", \"format\": \"CSV\"}\n  },\n  {\n    \"analysis_method\": \"Exposure, outcome and time-variable consistency check\",\n    \"operation\": \"Count violations of: pravastatin_exposed in {0,1} and equal to exposure_status=='pravastatin'; no excluded_other_statin rows; exposed rows have 0<=hours_to_first_pravastatin<=48 and unexposed rows have no pravastatin time; age>=18; death_28d, discharged_alive_before_28d in {0,1} and not both 1; event_status coded 1/2/0; 0<=followup_days<=28 with 28 for event_status 0; followup_end_time>=intime. Stop if any rule fails.\",\n    \"data_input\": {\"name\": \"cohort_imported.parquet\", \"format\": \"Parquet\"},\n    \"data_output\": {\"name\": \"value_validation.csv\", \"format\": \"CSV\"}\n  },\n  {\n    \"analysis_method\": \"Protocol-to-data and published-study concordance assessment\",\n    \"operation\": \"Tabulate each study-design element against available columns and against the approach of published MIMIC-IV statin-sepsis cohorts (Front Immunol 2025 doi:10.3389/fimmu.2025.1537172; Front Pharmacol 2025 doi:10.3389/fphar.2025.1610450 and doi:10.3389/fphar.2025.1520107; Front Neurol 2024 doi:10.3389/fneur.2024.1371314). Record: primary outcome is 28-day all-cause mortality from ICU admission using deathtime or dod (post-discharge deaths included, as in the published studies) instead of in-hospital death censored at discharge, which is kept as a design-specified secondary analysis; the primary analysis is 1:1 nearest-neighbour propensity-score matching (caliper 0.05 on the propensity-score scale, without replacement) followed by Cox regression in the matched cohort, with stabilized IPTW, overlap weighting and multivariable Cox models as sensitivity analyses; SAPS II, APS III and LODS are not available so SOFA is used; mechanical ventilation and RRT are not adjusted for because the design treats them as post-exposure; exposure within 48 h follows the published early-statin (48 h) design, and immortal time is examined with a 48-hour landmark and a time-dependent exposure Cox model.\",\n    \"data_input\": {\"name\": \"schema_validation.csv; value_validation.csv\", \"format\": \"CSV\"},\n    \"data_output\": {\"name\": \"protocol_concordance.csv\", \"format\": \"CSV\"}\n  },\n  {\n    \"analysis_method\": \"Analysis-variable specification\",\n    \"operation\": \"Write a JSON specification. Exposure: pravastatin_exposed. Primary outcome: time28_all/death28_all (28-day all-cause death from intime using deathtime, else dod at 12:00, complete follow-up to day 28). Secondary outcomes: time90_all/death90_all, hosp_death (hospital_expire_flag), icu_death (deathtime <= outtime + 6 h), icu_los_days (los), hosp_los_days; design-specified outcome followup_days/death_28d/event_status. PS covariates: continuous age, charlson_index, sofa_total_24h, hours_admit_to_icu, weight_kg, heart_rate_max, mbp_min, resp_rate_max, temperature_max, spo2_min, gcs_min, lactate_max, creatinine_max, platelets_min, wbc_max, hemoglobin_min, bicarbonate_min, bun_max, glucose_max, urine_output_24h_ml; binary female, cm_myocardial_infarction, cm_congestive_heart_failure, cm_peripheral_vascular, cm_cerebrovascular, cm_chronic_pulmonary, cm_renal, cm_malignancy, cm_metastatic_tumor, cm_severe_liver, cm_hypertension, cm_dyslipidemia, diabetes_any, prior_statin_use, has_prior_admission, med_vasopressor_24h, med_corticosteroid_24h, med_broad_abx_24h, med_insulin_24h; categorical race_group (ref White), insurance (ref Medicare), admission_type_grp (ref EW EMER.), first_careunit_grp (ref MICU), sepsis_category (ref sepsis). Log-transform lactate_max, creatinine_max, wbc_max, bun_max, glucose_max; log1p urine_output_24h_ml and hours_admit_to_icu (negative hours set to 0). Subgroups as in the published studies plus the design: age (<65, >=65), sex, sofa_tertile (SAPS II substitute), Charlson index (<3, >=3), septic shock (sepsis_category), organ_failure_any. Exclude post-baseline or outcome-defining variables and pf_ratio_min/sofa_respiration (~50% missing) from covariates.\",\n    \"data_input\": {\"name\": \"protocol_concordance.csv\", \"format\": \"CSV\"},\n    \"data_output\": {\"name\": \"analysis_variable_specification.json\", \"format\": \"JSON\"}\n  },\n  {\n    \"analysis_method\": \"Analysis cohort preparation\",\n    \"operation\": \"In DuckDB SQL derive the covariates of the specification (female, diabetes_any, grouped categories, insurance 'Unknown', urine output < 0 set to missing, log transforms), the subgroup variables, and the outcomes: death_time_all = coalesce(deathtime, dod + 12 h); death28_all = death_time_all <= intime + 28 days, time28_all = days from intime to min(death_time_all, intime + 28 days) floored at 0; likewise death90_all/time90_all; hosp_death = hospital_expire_flag; icu_death = deathtime <= outtime + 6 h; icu_los_days = los; hosp_los_days = (dischtime - admittime) in days. Keep the design-specified outcome columns. No rows are dropped.\",\n    \"data_input\": {\"name\": \"cohort_imported.parquet; analysis_variable_specification.json\", \"format\": \"Parquet and JSON\"},\n    \"data_output\": {\"name\": \"analysis_cohort.parquet\", \"format\": \"Parquet\"}\n  },\n  {\n    \"analysis_method\": \"Cohort accounting and crude outcomes\",\n    \"operation\": \"By exposure group and overall report n, 28-day and 90-day all-cause deaths with Wilson 95% CI, in-hospital and ICU deaths, median (IQR) ICU and hospital length of stay, design-specified in-hospital 28-day deaths, discharges alive before day 28, exposure timing (0-24 h vs 24-48 h) and deaths before 48 h.\",\n    \"data_input\": {\"name\": \"analysis_cohort.parquet\", \"format\": \"Parquet\"},\n    \"data_output\": {\"name\": \"cohort_outcome_counts.csv\", \"format\": \"CSV\"}\n  },\n  {\n    \"analysis_method\": \"Missing-data assessment\",\n    \"operation\": \"Missing count and percentage per specified covariate overall and by exposure group; flag covariates above 40% missing as not imputable (published studies excluded variables above 20-50% missing; none of the specified covariates exceeds 20%).\",\n    \"data_input\": {\"name\": \"analysis_cohort.parquet\", \"format\": \"Parquet\"},\n    \"data_output\": {\"name\": \"missingness_summary.csv\", \"format\": \"CSV\"}\n  },\n  {\n    \"analysis_method\": \"Multiple imputation by chained equations\",\n    \"operation\": \"Create m=20 imputations (20 iterations, seeds 20261120+k) of the continuous PS covariates on their transformed scale using chained Bayesian linear regression draws with exposure, death28_all, the Nelson-Aalen cumulative hazard at time28_all and all complete covariates as predictors; clip to the observed range; never impute exposure or outcomes. Save long format with an imputation index.\",\n    \"data_input\": {\"name\": \"analysis_cohort.parquet; missingness_summary.csv\", \"format\": \"Parquet and CSV\"},\n    \"data_output\": {\"name\": \"imputed_cohorts.parquet\", \"format\": \"Parquet\"}\n  },\n  {\n    \"analysis_method\": \"Unweighted baseline summary and standardized mean differences\",\n    \"operation\": \"On observed data by exposure group: mean, SD, median, IQR and missing n for continuous covariates; n (%) for binary covariates and categorical levels; absolute SMD with pooled SD.\",\n    \"data_input\": {\"name\": \"analysis_cohort.parquet\", \"format\": \"Parquet\"},\n    \"data_output\": {\"name\": \"baseline_unweighted.csv\", \"format\": \"CSV\"}\n  },\n  {\n    \"analysis_method\": \"Propensity-score estimation\",\n    \"operation\": \"Within each imputation fit a multivariable logistic regression of pravastatin_exposed on all PS covariates; record convergence, separation and C-statistic; if any imputation fails to converge or separates, refit all imputations with L2-penalized logistic regression (C=1.0).\",\n    \"data_input\": {\"name\": \"imputed_cohorts.parquet; analysis_variable_specification.json\", \"format\": \"Parquet and JSON\"},\n    \"data_output\": {\"name\": \"propensity_scores.parquet\", \"format\": \"Parquet\"}\n  },\n  {\n    \"analysis_method\": \"Propensity-score overlap assessment\",\n    \"operation\": \"Per imputation and exposure group report PS minimum, 1/5/50/95/99th percentiles, maximum and the number outside the other group's range; save 20-bin histogram counts for imputation 1.\",\n    \"data_input\": {\"name\": \"propensity_scores.parquet\", \"format\": \"Parquet\"},\n    \"data_output\": {\"name\": \"propensity_overlap.csv\", \"format\": \"CSV\"}\n  },\n  {\n    \"analysis_method\": \"1:1 nearest-neighbour propensity-score matching (primary design)\",\n    \"operation\": \"Within each imputation, as in the published MIMIC-IV statin-sepsis studies, match each pravastatin patient to one unexposed patient by greedy nearest-neighbour matching on the propensity score without replacement, processing exposed patients in descending PS order, with a caliper of 0.05 on the PS scale. Assign a pair_id to each matched pair, record unmatched exposed patients, and save the matched cohorts in long format.\",\n    \"data_input\": {\"name\": \"propensity_scores.parquet; imputed_cohorts.parquet\", \"format\": \"Parquet\"},\n    \"data_output\": {\"name\": \"matched_cohorts.parquet\", \"format\": \"Parquet\"}\n  },\n  {\n    \"analysis_method\": \"Matched-cohort balance assessment\",\n    \"operation\": \"Per imputation compute absolute SMDs of every covariate and categorical level in the matched cohort (pooled SD of the matched groups), average across imputations, classify balanced when the averaged SMD < 0.10, and report matched pairs and unmatched exposed patients per imputation.\",\n    \"data_input\": {\"name\": \"matched_cohorts.parquet\", \"format\": \"Parquet\"},\n    \"data_output\": {\"name\": \"matched_balance.csv\", \"format\": \"CSV\"}\n  },\n  {\n    \"analysis_method\": \"Stabilized IPTW construction (sensitivity design)\",\n    \"operation\": \"Within each imputation compute stabilized ATE weights p/PS for exposed and (1-p)/(1-PS) for unexposed (sw_raw), truncate at the 1st and 99th percentiles within each exposure group (sw), and also compute overlap weights (1-PS for exposed, PS for unexposed).\",\n    \"data_input\": {\"name\": \"propensity_scores.parquet; imputed_cohorts.parquet\", \"format\": \"Parquet\"},\n    \"data_output\": {\"name\": \"iptw_cohort.parquet\", \"format\": \"Parquet\"}\n  },\n  {\n    \"analysis_method\": \"Weight diagnostics and weighted balance\",\n    \"operation\": \"Per imputation and exposure group summarize sw, sw_raw and overlap weights (mean, SD, percentiles, maximum, effective sample size) and compute weighted SMDs for each weighting, averaged across imputations, with the 0.10 balance criterion.\",\n    \"data_input\": {\"name\": \"iptw_cohort.parquet\", \"format\": \"Parquet\"},\n    \"data_output\": {\"name\": \"iptw_diagnostics.csv; weighted_balance.csv\", \"format\": \"CSV\"}\n  },\n  {\n    \"analysis_method\": \"Publication-style Table 1 construction\",\n    \"operation\": \"Build Table 1 in the format of the published studies: per covariate, pravastatin and no-pravastatin summaries and SMD in the full cohort, then in the matched cohort (imputation 1 values for counts; SMD averaged over imputations), plus the IPTW SMD.\",\n    \"data_input\": {\"name\": \"baseline_unweighted.csv; matched_cohorts.parquet; matched_balance.csv; weighted_balance.csv\", \"format\": \"CSV and Parquet\"},\n    \"data_output\": {\"name\": \"table1_baseline_characteristics.csv\", \"format\": \"CSV\"}\n  },\n  {\n    \"analysis_method\": \"Kaplan-Meier survival in the matched cohort\",\n    \"operation\": \"Within each imputation's matched cohort estimate Kaplan-Meier survival to day 28 for the primary outcome by exposure group and the log-rank test; report survival on days 0-28 averaged over imputations, 28-day mortality by group and the median log-rank p-value; also report unmatched Kaplan-Meier curves.\",\n    \"data_input\": {\"name\": \"matched_cohorts.parquet; analysis_cohort.parquet\", \"format\": \"Parquet\"},\n    \"data_output\": {\"name\": \"km_survival_estimates.csv\", \"format\": \"CSV\"}\n  },\n  {\n    \"analysis_method\": \"Primary Cox regression in the matched cohort\",\n    \"operation\": \"Within each imputation's matched cohort fit a Cox proportional-hazards model of time28_all/death28_all on pravastatin_exposed with robust variance clustered on pair_id (Efron ties), pool log hazard ratios across imputations with Rubin's rules, and report the HR, 95% CI and p-value.\",\n    \"data_input\": {\"name\": \"matched_cohorts.parquet\", \"format\": \"Parquet\"},\n    \"data_output\": {\"name\": \"primary_cox_results.csv\", \"format\": \"CSV\"}\n  },\n  {\n    \"analysis_method\": \"Proportional-hazards assessment\",\n    \"operation\": \"Test the PH assumption for pravastatin_exposed in each imputation's primary matched Cox model with scaled Schoenfeld residuals (rank and log time) and report the median p-value; if it is below 0.05, report the 28-day risk difference and odds ratio from the matched cohort as the primary effect measure.\",\n    \"data_input\": {\"name\": \"matched_cohorts.parquet\", \"format\": \"Parquet\"},\n    \"data_output\": {\"name\": \"proportional_hazards_test.csv\", \"format\": \"CSV\"}\n  },\n  {\n    \"analysis_method\": \"Multivariable Cox models in the full cohort\",\n    \"operation\": \"As in the published studies, fit three Cox models of the primary outcome in the full cohort within each imputation and pool with Rubin's rules: Model 1 unadjusted; Model 2 adjusted for age, sex and race_group; Model 3 adjusted for all PS covariates.\",\n    \"data_input\": {\"name\": \"imputed_cohorts.parquet\", \"format\": \"Parquet\"},\n    \"data_output\": {\"name\": \"multivariable_cox_results.csv\", \"format\": \"CSV\"}\n  },\n  {\n    \"analysis_method\": \"Secondary outcomes in the matched cohort\",\n    \"operation\": \"In each imputation's matched cohort: Cox model for 90-day all-cause mortality (pair-clustered robust variance); logistic regression with pair-clustered sandwich variance for in-hospital mortality and ICU mortality (odds ratios); all pooled by Rubin's rules. Report median (IQR) ICU and hospital length of stay by group with the Mann-Whitney test in the imputation 1 matched cohort.\",\n    \"data_input\": {\"name\": \"matched_cohorts.parquet\", \"format\": \"Parquet\"},\n    \"data_output\": {\"name\": \"secondary_outcome_results.csv\", \"format\": \"CSV\"}\n  },\n  {\n    \"analysis_method\": \"Subgroup analyses\",\n    \"operation\": \"In each imputation's matched cohort fit pair-clustered Cox models with pravastatin_exposed, subgroup indicators and their interactions for age (<65, >=65), sex, sofa_tertile, Charlson index (<3, >=3), septic shock and organ_failure_any; pool stratum HRs with Rubin's rules and the interaction with a pooled multivariate Wald test; report strata with fewer than 5 deaths in either group as not_estimable.\",\n    \"data_input\": {\"name\": \"matched_cohorts.parquet\", \"format\": \"Parquet\"},\n    \"data_output\": {\"name\": \"subgroup_results.csv\", \"format\": \"CSV\"}\n  },\n  {\n    \"analysis_method\": \"Sensitivity analyses: alternative confounding control\",\n    \"operation\": \"Pooled Cox HRs for the primary outcome with: (a) stabilized truncated IPTW (design-specified ATE), (b) untruncated stabilized IPTW, (c) overlap weights, (d) 1:1 PSM with caliper 0.2 SD of the logit PS, (e) complete-case PSM without imputation, (f) PSM restricted to no prior statin use and (g) to prior statin use, re-estimating the PS in each subset. Report n, deaths and balance (maximum SMD) for each.\",\n    \"data_input\": {\"name\": \"iptw_cohort.parquet; analysis_cohort.parquet; analysis_variable_specification.json\", \"format\": \"Parquet and JSON\"},\n    \"data_output\": {\"name\": \"sensitivity_confounding_results.csv\", \"format\": \"CSV\"}\n  },\n  {\n    \"analysis_method\": \"Sensitivity analyses: immortal time\",\n    \"operation\": \"(h) 48-hour landmark: restrict to patients alive at 48 h (time28_all > 2), restart follow-up at the landmark, re-impute, re-estimate the PS, 1:1 PSM (caliper 0.05) and pair-clustered Cox, pooled. (i) Time-dependent exposure: in the full cohort split each patient's follow-up at hours_to_first_pravastatin so exposure switches from 0 to 1 at initiation, fit a time-varying Cox model adjusted for all PS covariates in each imputation, and pool.\",\n    \"data_input\": {\"name\": \"analysis_cohort.parquet; imputed_cohorts.parquet\", \"format\": \"Parquet\"},\n    \"data_output\": {\"name\": \"sensitivity_immortal_time_results.csv\", \"format\": \"CSV\"}\n  },\n  {\n    \"analysis_method\": \"Design-specified in-hospital outcome and competing risks\",\n    \"operation\": \"Using the design-specified outcome (followup_days, death_28d; patients discharged alive censored at discharge), fit the pair-clustered Cox model in the matched cohorts and a Fine-Gray model treating discharge alive (event_status 2) as the competing event (competing-event patients kept in the risk set to day 28 because the only censoring is administrative), with matched-cohort cumulative incidence of death at day 28; pool by Rubin's rules.\",\n    \"data_input\": {\"name\": \"matched_cohorts.parquet\", \"format\": \"Parquet\"},\n    \"data_output\": {\"name\": \"design_outcome_results.csv\", \"format\": \"CSV\"}\n  },\n  {\n    \"analysis_method\": \"Publication-style results table with E-value\",\n    \"operation\": \"Combine the primary, multivariable, secondary-outcome, sensitivity, design-outcome and subgroup results into Table 2 (analysis, population, outcome, n and deaths by group, effect measure, estimate, 95% CI, p-value, status, note), and add the E-value for the primary HR and its confidence limit closest to 1 using RR = (1-0.5^sqrt(HR))/(1-0.5^sqrt(1/HR)). Keep not_estimable rows without invented values.\",\n    \"data_input\": {\"name\": \"primary_cox_results.csv; multivariable_cox_results.csv; secondary_outcome_results.csv; sensitivity_confounding_results.csv; sensitivity_immortal_time_results.csv; design_outcome_results.csv; subgroup_results.csv\", \"format\": \"CSV\"},\n    \"data_output\": {\"name\": \"table2_mortality_associations.csv\", \"format\": \"CSV\"}\n  },\n  {\n    \"analysis_method\": \"Final standardized result packaging\",\n    \"operation\": \"Write an Excel workbook with sheets for protocol concordance, cohort counts, missingness, Table 1, PS overlap, matched balance, weight diagnostics, weighted balance, Kaplan-Meier estimates, PH test, Table 2 and subgroups, plus a matched-cohort Kaplan-Meier figure and a forest plot of main, sensitivity and subgroup HRs as PNG files.\",\n    \"data_input\": {\"name\": \"protocol_concordance.csv; cohort_outcome_counts.csv; missingness_summary.csv; table1_baseline_characteristics.csv; propensity_overlap.csv; matched_balance.csv; iptw_diagnostics.csv; weighted_balance.csv; km_survival_estimates.csv; proportional_hazards_test.csv; table2_mortality_associations.csv; subgroup_results.csv\", \"format\": \"CSV\"},\n    \"data_output\": {\"name\": \"pravastatin_28d_mortality_results.xlsx\", \"format\": \"XLSX\"}\n  }\n]\n"}, "runner": "\"\"\"\nRun every analysis step (a01 ... a26) in order.\n\nPlan   : ../output/exp_analysis_planning_final_cohort.json (one script per plan step)\nInput  : D:/mimic-iv-3.1/hosp.duckdb :: final_cohort_patient_level (read-only)\nOutput : ../output/analysis_output/\n\nUsage:\n    python run_analysis.py          # run all steps\n    python run_analysis.py 17       # start from step a17 (earlier outputs must exist)\n\"\"\"\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport time\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nSTEPS = sorted(HERE.glob(\"a[0-9][0-9]_*.py\"))\n\n\ndef main():\n    start = int(sys.argv[1]) if len(sys.argv) > 1 else 1\n    t0 = time.time()\n    for script in STEPS:\n        if int(script.name[1:3]) < start:\n            continue\n        print(f\"\\n===== {script.name} =====\", flush=True)\n        r = subprocess.run([sys.executable, \"-W\", \"ignore\", str(script)], cwd=HERE)\n        if r.returncode != 0:\n            print(f\"!! {script.name} failed (exit {r.returncode}); stopping.\")\n            sys.exit(r.returncode)\n    print(f\"\\nAll analysis steps finished in {time.time() - t0:.1f}s\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n", "common": "\"\"\"\nShared helpers for the analysis steps (a01 ... a26).\n\nPlan    : ../output/exp_analysis_planning_final_cohort.json\nInputs  : D:/mimic-iv-3.1/hosp.duckdb :: final_cohort_patient_level (opened read-only)\nOutputs : ../output/analysis_output/\n\nstatsmodels and scikit-learn are not installed in this Python, so the plan's\nstatsmodels Logit / GLM and sklearn IterativeImputer steps are implemented here with\nnumpy (IRLS logistic regression, HC0 sandwich variance, Bayesian-linear-regression\nchained equations).  Cox, Kaplan-Meier, Aalen-Johansen and the PH test use lifelines.\nParquet files are read and written with DuckDB (pyarrow is not installed).\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport json\nimport warnings\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport duckdb\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nfrom scipy import stats\n\nwarnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\", message=\".*weights are not integers.*\")\nwarnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\", category=FutureWarning)\n\nHOSP_DB = \"D:/mimic-iv-3.1/hosp.duckdb\"\nSOURCE_TABLE = \"final_cohort_patient_level\"\nBASE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\nOUT = BASE / \"output\" / \"analysis_output\"\nOUT.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n\nN_IMP = 20\nSEED_BASE = 20261120\nEXPOSURE = \"pravastatin_exposed\"\n# Primary outcome (as in published MIMIC-IV statin-sepsis cohorts): 28-day all-cause death\n# from ICU intime using deathtime or dod, with complete follow-up to day 28.\nDURATION = \"time28_all\"\nEVENT = \"death28_all\"\n# Design-specified outcome: in-hospital death, discharged alive censored at discharge.\nDESIGN_DURATION = \"followup_days\"\nDESIGN_EVENT = \"death_28d\"\nCALIPER_PS = 0.05          # primary 1:1 PSM caliper on the PS scale (published studies)\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- I/O\ndef path(name: str) -> Path:\n    return OUT / name\n\n\ndef sql_path(name: str) -> str:\n    return str(path(name)).replace(\"\\\\\", \"/\")\n\n\ndef con_mem() -> duckdb.DuckDBPyConnection:\n    return duckdb.connect()\n\n\ndef read_parquet(name: str) -> pd.DataFrame:\n    with duckdb.connect() as con:\n        return con.execute(f\"SELECT * FROM read_parquet('{sql_path(name)}')\").df()\n\n\ndef write_parquet(df: pd.DataFrame, name: str) -> None:\n    with duckdb.connect() as con:\n        con.register(\"df_out\", df)\n        con.execute(f\"COPY df_out TO '{sql_path(name)}' (FORMAT parquet)\")\n\n\ndef read_csv(name: str) -> pd.DataFrame:\n    return pd.read_csv(path(name))\n\n\ndef write_csv(df: pd.DataFrame, name: str) -> None:\n    df.to_csv(path(name), index=False, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n\n\ndef read_json(name: str):\n    return json.loads(path(name).read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n\n\ndef write_json(obj, name: str) -> None:\n    path(name).write_text(json.dumps(obj, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n\n\ndef log(step: str, msg: str) -> None:\n    print(f\"[{step}] {msg}\", flush=True)\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------- design matrix\ndef spec() -> dict:\n    return read_json(\"analysis_variable_specification.json\")\n\n\ndef model_continuous(sp: dict) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"Names of continuous model columns (transformed names where applicable).\"\"\"\n    return [sp[\"transformed_names\"].get(c, c) for c in sp[\"ps_covariates\"][\"continuous\"]]\n\n\ndef design_matrix(df: pd.DataFrame, sp: dict, drop: tuple = ()) -> tuple[np.ndarray, list[str]]:\n    \"\"\"Main-effects PS design (no intercept). Continuous columns are z-scored.\"\"\"\n    cols, names = [], []\n    for c in model_continuous(sp):\n        if c in drop:\n            continue\n        x = df[c].astype(float).to_numpy()\n        sd = x.std()\n        cols.append((x - x.mean()) / sd if sd > 0 else x * 0)\n        names.append(c)\n    for c in sp[\"ps_covariates\"][\"binary\"]:\n        if c in drop:\n            continue\n        cols.append(df[c].astype(float).to_numpy())\n        names.append(c)\n    for c, ref in sp[\"ps_covariates\"][\"categorical\"].items():\n        if c in drop:\n            continue\n        for lev in sorted(df[c].dropna().unique()):\n            if lev == ref:\n                continue\n            cols.append((df[c] == lev).astype(float).to_numpy())\n            names.append(f\"{c}[{lev}]\")\n    X = np.column_stack(cols)\n    keep = X.std(axis=0) > 0          # drop constant columns (e.g. restricted samples)\n    return X[:, keep], [n for n, k in zip(names, keep) if k]\n\n\ndef balance_columns(df: pd.DataFrame, sp: dict) -> dict[str, np.ndarray]:\n    \"\"\"Covariates on the reporting scale for SMDs (original continuous, binaries, levels).\"\"\"\n    out = {}\n    for c in sp[\"ps_covariates\"][\"continuous\"]:\n        out[c] = df[c].astype(float).to_numpy()\n    for c in sp[\"ps_covariates\"][\"binary\"]:\n        out[c] = df[c].astype(float).to_numpy()\n    for c in sp[\"ps_covariates\"][\"categorical\"]:\n        for lev in sorted(df[c].dropna().unique()):\n            out[f\"{c}={lev}\"] = (df[c] == lev).astype(float).to_numpy()\n    return out\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------ logistic / GLM\ndef fit_logistic(X: np.ndarray, y: np.ndarray, l2: float = 0.0, max_iter: int = 100,\n                 tol: float = 1e-8) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Newton-Raphson (IRLS) logistic regression with intercept; optional L2 (not on intercept).\"\"\"\n    Xd = np.column_stack([np.ones(len(y)), X])\n    beta = np.zeros(Xd.shape[1])\n    pen = np.full(Xd.shape[1], l2)\n    pen[0] = 0.0\n    converged = False\n    for it in range(max_iter):\n        eta = np.clip(Xd @ beta, -35, 35)\n        p = 1 / (1 + np.exp(-eta))\n        W = p * (1 - p)\n        grad = Xd.T @ (y - p) - pen * beta\n        H = (Xd * W[:, None]).T @ Xd + np.diag(pen)\n        step = np.linalg.solve(H, grad)\n        beta += step\n        if np.max(np.abs(step)) < tol:\n            converged = True\n            break\n    eta = np.clip(Xd @ beta, -35, 35)\n    p = 1 / (1 + np.exp(-eta))\n    separation = bool(np.max(np.abs(beta[1:])) > 15 or np.mean((p < 1e-8) | (p > 1 - 1e-8)) > 0)\n    return {\"beta\": beta, \"p\": p, \"converged\": converged, \"iterations\": it + 1,\n            \"separation\": separation}\n\n\ndef c_statistic(y: np.ndarray, score: np.ndarray) -> float:\n    r = stats.rankdata(score)\n    n1 = y.sum()\n    n0 = len(y) - n1\n    return float((r[y == 1].sum() - n1 * (n1 + 1) / 2) / (n1 * n0))\n\n\ndef weighted_logit_hc0(y: np.ndarray, x: np.ndarray, w: np.ndarray,\n                       cluster: np.ndarray | None = None) -> tuple[float, float]:\n    \"\"\"GLM Binomial(logit) of y on [1, x] with var_weights=w; returns (beta_x, sandwich variance).\n\n    HC0 when cluster is None, otherwise cluster-robust (e.g. matched pair_id).\n    \"\"\"\n    Xd = np.column_stack([np.ones(len(y)), x])\n    beta = np.zeros(2)\n    for _ in range(100):\n        p = 1 / (1 + np.exp(-(Xd @ beta)))\n        grad = Xd.T @ (w * (y - p))\n        H = (Xd * (w * p * (1 - p))[:, None]).T @ Xd\n        step = np.linalg.solve(H, grad)\n        beta += step\n        if np.max(np.abs(step)) < 1e-10:\n            break\n    p = 1 / (1 + np.exp(-(Xd @ beta)))\n    bread = np.linalg.inv((Xd * (w * p * (1 - p))[:, None]).T @ Xd)\n    scores = Xd * (w * (y - p))[:, None]\n    if cluster is not None:\n        scores = pd.DataFrame(scores).groupby(np.asarray(cluster)).sum().to_numpy()\n    meat = scores.T @ scores\n    V = bread @ meat @ bread\n    return float(beta[1]), float(V[1, 1])\n\n\ndef weighted_risk(y: np.ndarray, w: np.ndarray) -> tuple[float, float]:\n    \"\"\"Weighted mean and its sandwich variance (weights treated as fixed).\"\"\"\n    p = np.sum(w * y) / np.sum(w)\n    var = np.sum(w ** 2 * (y - p) ** 2) / np.sum(w) ** 2\n    return float(p), float(var)\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------- IPTW tools\ndef stabilized_weights(a: np.ndarray, ps: np.ndarray, truncate: bool = True) -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n    \"\"\"Stabilized ATE weights; truncation at the 1st/99th percentiles WITHIN each exposure group.\n\n    (Pooled-distribution truncation, as first written in the plan, clips almost every exposed\n    weight when exposure prevalence is ~2.5%, so the percentiles are taken per group.)\n    \"\"\"\n    pm = a.mean()\n    raw = np.where(a == 1, pm / ps, (1 - pm) / (1 - ps))\n    if not truncate:\n        return raw, raw\n    sw = raw.copy()\n    for g in (0, 1):\n        m = a == g\n        lo, hi = np.percentile(raw[m], [1, 99])\n        sw[m] = np.clip(raw[m], lo, hi)\n    return raw, sw\n\n\ndef alternative_weights(a: np.ndarray, ps: np.ndarray, kind: str) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"ATT weights (1 / PS/(1-PS)) or overlap weights (1-PS / PS) for sensitivity analyses.\"\"\"\n    if kind == \"att\":\n        return np.where(a == 1, 1.0, ps / (1 - ps))\n    if kind == \"overlap\":\n        return np.where(a == 1, 1 - ps, ps)\n    raise ValueError(kind)\n\n\ndef smd(x: np.ndarray, a: np.ndarray, w: np.ndarray | None = None,\n        pooled_sd: float | None = None) -> float:\n    ok = ~np.isnan(x)\n    x, a = x[ok], a[ok]\n    w = np.ones_like(x) if w is None else w[ok]\n    m1 = np.average(x[a == 1], weights=w[a == 1])\n    m0 = np.average(x[a == 0], weights=w[a == 0])\n    if pooled_sd is None:\n        pooled_sd = np.sqrt((x[a == 1].var(ddof=1) + x[a == 0].var(ddof=1)) / 2)\n    return float(abs(m1 - m0) / pooled_sd) if pooled_sd > 0 else 0.0\n\n\ndef ess(w: np.ndarray) -> float:\n    return float(w.sum() ** 2 / np.sum(w ** 2))\n\n\ndef ps_and_weights(df: pd.DataFrame, sp: dict, drop: tuple = ()) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"PS model with prespecified ridge fallback, then stabilized truncated weights.\"\"\"\n    X, names = design_matrix(df, sp, drop)\n    a = df[EXPOSURE].to_numpy().astype(float)\n    fit = fit_logistic(X, a)\n    method = \"unpenalized_logit\"\n    if not fit[\"converged\"] or fit[\"separation\"]:\n        fit = fit_logistic(X, a, l2=1.0)\n        method = \"ridge_logit_C1_fallback\"\n    ps = fit[\"p\"]\n    raw, sw = stabilized_weights(a, ps)\n    return {\"ps\": ps, \"sw_raw\": raw, \"sw\": sw, \"method\": method,\n            \"converged\": fit[\"converged\"], \"separation\": fit[\"separation\"],\n            \"c_statistic\": c_statistic(a, ps), \"n_params\": X.shape[1]}\n\n\ndef match_1to1(a: np.ndarray, ps: np.ndarray, caliper: float, scale: str = \"ps\") -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n    \"\"\"Greedy 1:1 nearest-neighbour matching without replacement.\n\n    Exposed units are processed in descending PS order (MatchIt default m.order='largest').\n    scale='ps' applies the caliper on the PS scale; scale='logit' on the logit-PS scale.\n    Returns (treated_index, control_index) arrays of matched positions.\n    \"\"\"\n    s = np.log(ps / (1 - ps)) if scale == \"logit\" else ps\n    treated = np.where(a == 1)[0]\n    treated = treated[np.argsort(-ps[treated], kind=\"stable\")]\n    controls = np.where(a == 0)[0]\n    avail = np.ones(len(controls), bool)\n    cs = s[controls]\n    t_idx, c_idx = [], []\n    for t in treated:\n        dist = np.where(avail, np.abs(cs - s[t]), np.inf)\n        j = int(np.argmin(dist))\n        if dist[j] <= caliper:\n            avail[j] = False\n            t_idx.append(t)\n            c_idx.append(controls[j])\n    return np.array(t_idx, int), np.array(c_idx, int)\n\n\ndef matched_frame(d: pd.DataFrame, ps: np.ndarray, caliper: float = CALIPER_PS,\n                  scale: str = \"ps\") -> pd.DataFrame:\n    \"\"\"Matched rows of d with pair_id; d must be positionally aligned with ps.\"\"\"\n    d = d.reset_index(drop=True)\n    t, c = match_1to1(d[EXPOSURE].to_numpy(), ps, caliper, scale)\n    m = pd.concat([d.iloc[t].assign(pair_id=np.arange(len(t))),\n                   d.iloc[c].assign(pair_id=np.arange(len(c)))], ignore_index=True)\n    m[\"ps\"] = np.concatenate([ps[t], ps[c]])\n    return m\n\n\ndef max_smd_unweighted(df: pd.DataFrame, sp: dict) -> float:\n    a = df[EXPOSURE].to_numpy()\n    return float(np.nanmax([smd(x, a) for x in balance_columns(df, sp).values()]))\n\n\ndef max_weighted_smd(df: pd.DataFrame, sp: dict, w: np.ndarray) -> float:\n    a = df[EXPOSURE].to_numpy()\n    vals = [smd(x, a, w) for x in balance_columns(df, sp).values()]\n    return float(np.nanmax(vals))\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------- Cox\ndef cox_exposure(df: pd.DataFrame, duration: str, event: str, weight: str | None,\n                 covariates: list[str] | None = None, cluster: str | None = None) -> tuple[float, float, object]:\n    \"\"\"Cox model (Efron ties, robust variance, optionally clustered); returns (log HR, variance, fitter).\"\"\"\n    from lifelines import CoxPHFitter\n    cols = [duration, event, EXPOSURE] + (covariates or []) + ([weight] if weight else []) \\\n        + ([cluster] if cluster else [])\n    d = df[cols].copy()\n    cph = CoxPHFitter(penalizer=0.0)\n    cph.fit(d, duration_col=duration, event_col=event, weights_col=weight, robust=True,\n            cluster_col=cluster)\n    b = float(cph.params_[EXPOSURE])\n    v = float(cph.variance_matrix_.loc[EXPOSURE, EXPOSURE])\n    return b, v, cph\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------- Rubin's rules\ndef rubin(est, var, n_obs: int, k_params: int = 1) -> dict:\n    est, var = np.asarray(est, float), np.asarray(var, float)\n    m = len(est)\n    qbar = est.mean()\n    ubar = var.mean()\n    b = est.var(ddof=1) if m > 1 else 0.0\n    t = ubar + (1 + 1 / m) * b\n    nu_com = n_obs - k_params\n    if m > 1 and b > 0:\n        lam = (1 + 1 / m) * b / t\n        nu_old = (m - 1) / lam ** 2\n        nu_obs = (nu_com + 1) / (nu_com + 3) * nu_com * (1 - lam)\n        df = 1 / (1 / nu_old + 1 / nu_obs)\n    else:\n        df = nu_com\n    se = np.sqrt(t)\n    tcrit = stats.t.ppf(0.975, df)\n    p = 2 * stats.t.sf(abs(qbar / se), df)\n    return {\"est\": qbar, \"se\": se, \"lo\": qbar - tcrit * se, \"hi\": qbar + tcrit * se,\n            \"p\": p, \"df\": df, \"m\": m, \"fmi_lambda\": ((1 + 1 / m) * b / t) if t > 0 else 0.0}\n\n\ndef rubin_wald(ests: list[np.ndarray], covs: list[np.ndarray]) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Multivariate pooled Wald test (D1, Li-Raghunathan-Rubin).\"\"\"\n    Q = np.array(ests)\n    m, k = Q.shape\n    qbar = Q.mean(axis=0)\n    U = np.mean(covs, axis=0)\n    B = np.cov(Q.T, ddof=1).reshape(k, k) if m > 1 else np.zeros((k, k))\n    Uinv = np.linalg.inv(U)\n    r = (1 + 1 / m) * np.trace(B @ Uinv) / k\n    D1 = float(qbar @ Uinv @ qbar / (k * (1 + r)))\n    t = k * (m - 1)\n    if r <= 0:\n        v = np.inf\n    elif t > 4:\n        v = 4 + (t - 4) * (1 + (1 - 2 / t) / r) ** 2\n    else:\n        v = t * (1 + 1 / k) * (1 + 1 / r) ** 2 / 2\n    p = float(stats.f.sf(D1, k, v)) if np.isfinite(v) else float(stats.chi2.sf(D1 * k, k))\n    return {\"D1\": D1, \"df1\": k, \"df2\": v, \"p\": p}\n\n\ndef hr_row(analysis: str, res: dict, **extra) -> dict:\n    row = {\"analysis\": analysis, \"effect_measure\": \"HR\", \"estimate\": np.exp(res[\"est\"]),\n           \"ci_low\": np.exp(res[\"lo\"]), \"ci_high\": np.exp(res[\"hi\"]), \"p_value\": res[\"p\"],\n           \"status\": \"estimated\"}\n    row.update(extra)\n    return row\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------- MICE\ndef nelson_aalen(df: pd.DataFrame, duration: str = DURATION, event: str = EVENT) -> np.ndarray:\n    from lifelines import NelsonAalenFitter\n    naf = NelsonAalenFitter().fit(df[duration], df[event])\n    return naf.cumulative_hazard_at_times(df[duration]).to_numpy()\n\n\ndef mice(df: pd.DataFrame, sp: dict, m: int = N_IMP, iters: int = 20,\n         duration: str = DURATION, event: str = EVENT, seed_base: int = SEED_BASE) -> pd.DataFrame:\n    \"\"\"Chained equations with Bayesian linear regression draws (normal model, mice 'norm').\n\n    Imputes only the continuous PS covariates (transformed scale), clipped to the observed\n    range. Predictors: complete binary / one-hot covariates, exposure, outcome and the\n    Nelson-Aalen cumulative hazard. Returns long format with column 'imputation' (1..m).\n    \"\"\"\n    cont = model_continuous(sp)\n    base = df.reset_index(drop=True).copy()\n    aux = [base[EXPOSURE].astype(float).to_numpy(), base[event].astype(float).to_numpy(),\n           nelson_aalen(base, duration, event)]\n    for c in sp[\"ps_covariates\"][\"binary\"]:\n        aux.append(base[c].astype(float).to_numpy())\n    for c, ref in sp[\"ps_covariates\"][\"categorical\"].items():\n        for lev in sorted(base[c].dropna().unique()):\n            if lev != ref:\n                aux.append((base[c] == lev).astype(float).to_numpy())\n    A = np.column_stack(aux)\n    Y0 = base[cont].astype(float).to_numpy()\n    miss = np.isnan(Y0)\n    targets = [j for j in range(len(cont)) if miss[:, j].any()]\n    lo = np.nanmin(Y0, axis=0)\n    hi = np.nanmax(Y0, axis=0)\n    out = []\n    for k in range(1, m + 1):\n        rng = np.random.default_rng(seed_base + k)\n        Y = Y0.copy()\n        for j in targets:                         # start from observed-value draws\n            obs = Y0[~miss[:, j], j]\n            Y[miss[:, j], j] = rng.choice(obs, miss[:, j].sum())\n        for _ in range(iters):\n            for j in targets:\n                others = np.delete(Y, j, axis=1)\n                Xf = np.column_stack([np.ones(len(Y)), A, others])\n                mu, sd = Xf[:, 1:].mean(0), Xf[:, 1:].std(0)\n                sd[sd == 0] = 1\n                Xf[:, 1:] = (Xf[:, 1:] - mu) / sd\n                o = ~miss[:, j]\n                Xo, yo = Xf[o], Y[o, j]\n                XtX = Xo.T @ Xo + 1e-5 * np.eye(Xo.shape[1])\n                V = np.linalg.inv(XtX)\n                bhat = V @ Xo.T @ yo\n                rss = np.sum((yo - Xo @ bhat) ** 2)\n                sigma2 = rss / rng.chisquare(o.sum() - Xo.shape[1])\n                bdraw = rng.multivariate_normal(bhat, V * sigma2)\n                Xm = Xf[~o]\n                Y[~o, j] = np.clip(Xm @ bdraw + rng.normal(0, np.sqrt(sigma2), len(Xm)),\n                                   lo[j], hi[j])\n        d = base.copy()\n        d[cont] = Y\n        for c in sp[\"ps_covariates\"][\"continuous\"]:     # back-transform reporting scale\n            t = sp[\"transformed_names\"].get(c)\n            if t:\n                f = sp[\"transforms\"][c]\n                d[c] = np.expm1(d[t]) if f == \"log1p\" else np.exp(d[t])\n        d.insert(0, \"imputation\", k)\n        out.append(d)\n    return pd.concat(out, ignore_index=True)\n", "steps": [{"step": 1, "file": "a01_data_import.py", "code": "\"\"\"\nAnalysis step 1. Data import\n\nInput     : D:/mimic-iv-3.1/hosp.duckdb :: final_cohort_patient_level (attached READ_ONLY)\nOperation : Copy the table unchanged (SELECT *) to Parquet. Nothing is written to the DuckDB file.\nOutput    : analysis_output/cohort_imported.parquet\n\"\"\"\nimport time\n\nfrom common import HOSP_DB, SOURCE_TABLE, con_mem, log, sql_path\n\nOUT_FILE = sql_path(\"cohort_imported.parquet\")\n\nSQL = f\"\"\"\nATTACH '{HOSP_DB}' AS hosp (READ_ONLY);\nCOPY (SELECT * FROM hosp.{SOURCE_TABLE}) TO '{OUT_FILE}' (FORMAT parquet);\n\"\"\"\n\n\ndef main():\n    t0 = time.time()\n    con = con_mem()\n    con.execute(SQL)\n    n = con.execute(f\"SELECT COUNT(*) FROM read_parquet('{OUT_FILE}')\").fetchone()[0]\n    k = len(con.execute(f\"DESCRIBE SELECT * FROM read_parquet('{OUT_FILE}')\").fetchall())\n    log(\"a01\", f\"cohort_imported.parquet rows={n:,} columns={k} ({time.time() - t0:.1f}s)\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n", "outputs": [{"name": "cohort_imported.parquet", "kind": "parquet", "exists": true, "bytes": 2181146, "rows": 9902, "columns": [{"name": "subject_id", "type": "BIGINT"}, {"name": "hadm_id", "type": "BIGINT"}, {"name": "stay_id", "type": "BIGINT"}, {"name": "first_careunit", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "last_careunit", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "intime", "type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "outtime", "type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "los", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "gender", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "anchor_age", "type": "BIGINT"}, {"name": "anchor_year", "type": "BIGINT"}, {"name": "anchor_year_group", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "dod", "type": "DATE"}, {"name": "birth_year", "type": "BIGINT"}, {"name": "age_at_intime", "type": "BIGINT"}, {"name": "admittime", "type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "dischtime", "type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "deathtime", "type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "hospital_expire_flag", "type": "BIGINT"}, {"name": "admission_type", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "admission_location", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "discharge_location", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "insurance", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "race", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "marital_status", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "language", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "sepsis_category", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "n_sepsis_codes", "type": "BIGINT"}, {"name": "has_positive_culture", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "first_positive_culture_time", "type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "has_broad_abx_48h", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "first_broad_abx_time", "type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "first_pravastatin_time", "type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "hours_to_first_pravastatin", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "n_pravastatin_orders", "type": "BIGINT"}, {"name": "exposure_status", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "pravastatin_exposed", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "death_time", "type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "admin_end_time", "type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "death_28d", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "discharged_alive_before_28d", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "followup_end_time", "type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "followup_days", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "event_status", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "n_qualifying_stays", "type": "BIGINT"}, {"name": "age", "type": "BIGINT"}, {"name": "sex", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "race_group", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "hours_admit_to_icu", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "has_prior_admission", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "n_prior_admissions", "type": "BIGINT"}, {"name": "cm_myocardial_infarction", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_congestive_heart_failure", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_peripheral_vascular", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_cerebrovascular", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_dementia", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_chronic_pulmonary", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_rheumatic", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_peptic_ulcer", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_mild_liver", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_diabetes_uncomplicated", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_diabetes_complicated", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_paraplegia", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_renal", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_malignancy", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_severe_liver", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_metastatic_tumor", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_hiv_aids", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_hypertension", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_dyslipidemia", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "heart_rate_min", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "heart_rate_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "heart_rate_mean", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "sbp_min", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "sbp_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "sbp_mean", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "dbp_min", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "dbp_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "dbp_mean", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "mbp_min", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "mbp_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "mbp_mean", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "resp_rate_min", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "resp_rate_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "resp_rate_mean", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "temperature_min", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "temperature_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "temperature_mean", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "spo2_min", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "spo2_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "spo2_mean", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "weight_kg", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "gcs_min", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "gcs_motor_min", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "creatinine_min", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "creatinine_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "bilirubin_min", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "bilirubin_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "platelets_min", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "platelets_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "wbc_min", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "wbc_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "lactate_min", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "lactate_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "hemoglobin_min", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "hemoglobin_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "bicarbonate_min", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "bicarbonate_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "sodium_min", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "sodium_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "potassium_min", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "potassium_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "bun_min", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "bun_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "glucose_min", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "glucose_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "inr_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "pf_ratio_min", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "urine_output_24h_ml", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "norepinephrine_max_rate", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "epinephrine_max_rate", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "dopamine_max_rate", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "dobutamine_max_rate", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "vasopressin_max_rate", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "phenylephrine_max_rate", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "med_vasopressor_24h", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "med_corticosteroid_24h", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "med_broad_abx_24h", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "med_insulin_24h", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "charlson_index", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "sofa_respiration", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "sofa_coagulation", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "sofa_liver", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "sofa_cardiovascular", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "sofa_cns", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "sofa_renal", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "sofa_total_24h", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "sofa_n_components_observed", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "n_organ_failures_24h", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "prior_statin_use", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "prior_pravastatin_use", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "n_prior_statin_orders", "type": "BIGINT"}, {"name": "first_prior_statin_time", "type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "last_prior_statin_time", "type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "days_since_last_prior_statin", "type": "BIGINT"}, {"name": "prior_statin_names", "type": "VARCHAR"}]}]}, {"step": 2, "file": "a02_schema_validation.py", "code": "\"\"\"\nAnalysis step 2. Schema and identifier validation\n\nInput     : cohort_imported.parquet\nOperation : Row/column counts (expect 9902 x 146), per-column dtype and missing count,\n            identifier checks: subject_id, stay_id nonmissing and unique; hadm_id nonmissing.\n            Stops (exit 1) if any identifier or shape check fails.\nOutput    : schema_validation.csv\n\"\"\"\nimport sys\n\nimport pandas as pd\n\nfrom common import con_mem, log, sql_path, write_csv\n\nSRC = f\"read_parquet('{sql_path('cohort_imported.parquet')}')\"\nEXPECTED_ROWS, EXPECTED_COLS = 9902, 146\n\n\ndef main():\n    con = con_mem()\n    desc = con.execute(f\"DESCRIBE SELECT * FROM {SRC}\").df()[[\"column_name\", \"column_type\"]]\n    miss_sql = \", \".join(f'COUNT(*) - COUNT(\"{c}\") AS \"{c}\"' for c in desc.column_name)\n    miss = con.execute(f\"SELECT {miss_sql} FROM {SRC}\").df().iloc[0]\n    rows = [{\"check\": \"column\", \"item\": r.column_name, \"observed_dtype\": r.column_type,\n             \"value\": int(miss[r.column_name]), \"expected\": \"\", \"status\": \"present\"}\n            for r in desc.itertuples()]\n\n    id_sql = f\"\"\"\n    SELECT 'n_rows' AS item, COUNT(*) AS value, {EXPECTED_ROWS} AS expected FROM {SRC}\n    UNION ALL SELECT 'n_columns', {len(desc)}, {EXPECTED_COLS}\n    UNION ALL SELECT 'subject_id_missing', COUNT(*) - COUNT(subject_id), 0 FROM {SRC}\n    UNION ALL SELECT 'subject_id_duplicated', COUNT(subject_id) - COUNT(DISTINCT subject_id), 0 FROM {SRC}\n    UNION ALL SELECT 'stay_id_missing', COUNT(*) - COUNT(stay_id), 0 FROM {SRC}\n    UNION ALL SELECT 'stay_id_duplicated', COUNT(stay_id) - COUNT(DISTINCT stay_id), 0 FROM {SRC}\n    UNION ALL SELECT 'hadm_id_missing', COUNT(*) - COUNT(hadm_id), 0 FROM {SRC}\n    \"\"\"\n    ids = con.execute(id_sql).df()\n    ids[\"status\"] = (ids.value == ids.expected).map({True: \"pass\", False: \"fail\"})\n    for r in ids.itertuples():\n        rows.append({\"check\": \"identifier/shape\", \"item\": r.item, \"observed_dtype\": \"\",\n                     \"value\": int(r.value), \"expected\": int(r.expected), \"status\": r.status})\n    write_csv(pd.DataFrame(rows), \"schema_validation.csv\")\n    fails = ids[ids.status == \"fail\"]\n    log(\"a02\", f\"columns={len(desc)}; identifier/shape checks failed={len(fails)}\")\n    if len(fails):\n        print(fails.to_string(index=False))\n        sys.exit(1)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n", "outputs": [{"name": "schema_validation.csv", "kind": "csv", "exists": true, "bytes": 6568, "rows": 153, "columns": [{"name": "check", "type": ""}, {"name": "item", "type": ""}, {"name": "observed_dtype", "type": ""}, {"name": "value", "type": ""}, {"name": "expected", "type": ""}, {"name": "status", "type": ""}]}]}, {"step": 3, "file": "a03_value_validation.py", "code": "\"\"\"\nAnalysis step 3. Exposure, outcome and time-variable consistency check\n\nInput     : cohort_imported.parquet\nOperation : One SQL rule per row counting violating records (exposure coding, 48-h window,\n            age, outcome flags, event_status coding, follow-up range, admin censoring at 28 d).\n            Stops (exit 1) if any rule fails.\nOutput    : value_validation.csv\n\"\"\"\nimport sys\n\nimport pandas as pd\n\nfrom common import con_mem, log, sql_path, write_csv\n\nSRC = f\"read_parquet('{sql_path('cohort_imported.parquet')}')\"\n\nRULES = [\n    (\"pravastatin_exposed in {0,1}\",\n     \"pravastatin_exposed IS NULL OR pravastatin_exposed NOT IN (0, 1)\"),\n    (\"pravastatin_exposed equals exposure_status = pravastatin\",\n     \"pravastatin_exposed <> CASE WHEN exposure_status = 'pravastatin' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END\"),\n    (\"no excluded_other_statin rows\",\n     \"exposure_status = 'excluded_other_statin'\"),\n    (\"exposed: hours_to_first_pravastatin in [0, 48] and time present\",\n     \"pravastatin_exposed = 1 AND (hours_to_first_pravastatin IS NULL OR first_pravastatin_time IS NULL \"\n     \"OR hours_to_first_pravastatin < 0 OR hours_to_first_pravastatin > 48)\"),\n    (\"unexposed: no pravastatin time\",\n     \"pravastatin_exposed = 0 AND (hours_to_first_pravastatin IS NOT NULL OR first_pravastatin_time IS NOT NULL)\"),\n    (\"age >= 18\", \"age IS NULL OR age < 18\"),\n    (\"death_28d in {0,1}\", \"death_28d IS NULL OR death_28d NOT IN (0, 1)\"),\n    (\"discharged_alive_before_28d in {0,1}\",\n     \"discharged_alive_before_28d IS NULL OR discharged_alive_before_28d NOT IN (0, 1)\"),\n    (\"death_28d and discharged_alive_before_28d not both 1\",\n     \"death_28d = 1 AND discharged_alive_before_28d = 1\"),\n    (\"event_status coding (1 death, 2 discharge alive, 0 otherwise)\",\n     \"event_status IS DISTINCT FROM CASE WHEN death_28d = 1 THEN 1 \"\n     \"WHEN discharged_alive_before_28d = 1 THEN 2 ELSE 0 END\"),\n    (\"followup_days in [0, 28]\",\n     \"followup_days IS NULL OR followup_days < 0 OR followup_days > 28\"),\n    (\"event_status 0 has followup_days = 28\",\n     \"event_status = 0 AND abs(followup_days - 28) > 1e-6\"),\n    (\"followup_end_time >= intime\", \"followup_end_time < intime\"),\n]\n\n\ndef main():\n    con = con_mem()\n    rows = []\n    for name, cond in RULES:\n        n = con.execute(f\"SELECT COUNT(*) FROM {SRC} WHERE {cond}\").fetchone()[0]\n        rows.append({\"rule\": name, \"sql_condition\": cond, \"n_violations\": int(n),\n                     \"status\": \"pass\" if n == 0 else \"fail\"})\n    out = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n    write_csv(out, \"value_validation.csv\")\n    n_fail = int((out.status == \"fail\").sum())\n    log(\"a03\", f\"rules={len(out)} failed={n_fail}\")\n    if n_fail:\n        print(out[out.status == \"fail\"][[\"rule\", \"n_violations\"]].to_string(index=False))\n        sys.exit(1)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n", "outputs": [{"name": "value_validation.csv", "kind": "csv", "exists": true, "bytes": 1570, "rows": 13, "columns": [{"name": "rule", "type": ""}, {"name": "sql_condition", "type": ""}, {"name": "n_violations", "type": ""}, {"name": "status", "type": ""}]}]}, {"step": 4, "file": "a04_protocol_concordance.py", "code": "\"\"\"\nAnalysis step 4. Protocol-to-data concordance assessment\n\nInput     : schema_validation.csv, value_validation.csv\nOperation : Map each study-design element to available columns, mark availability,\n            and record deviations (SAPS II -> SOFA tertiles, one stay per patient,\n            immortal time up to 48 h, 24-h baseline window overlapping early exposure).\nOutput    : protocol_concordance.csv\n\"\"\"\nimport pandas as pd\n\nfrom common import log, read_csv, write_csv\n\nELEMENTS = [\n    (\"population\", \"adult septic ICU patients\",\n     \"age;sepsis_category;has_positive_culture;has_broad_abx_48h\", \"as designed\", \"\"),\n    (\"exposure\", \"pravastatin initiated within 48 h of ICU intime\",\n     \"pravastatin_exposed;hours_to_first_pravastatin\", \"as designed\", \"\"),\n    (\"exclusion\", \"other statin within the same 48 h excluded\", \"exposure_status\", \"as designed\",\n     \"excluded upstream (preprocessing step08)\"),\n    (\"comparator\", \"no pravastatin within 48 h\", \"pravastatin_exposed\", \"as designed\", \"\"),\n    (\"outcome (primary)\", \"28-day all-cause mortality from ICU intime\", \"deathtime;dod;intime\", \"aligned with published studies\",\n     \"death from deathtime, else dod (post-discharge deaths included), complete follow-up to day 28; \"\n     \"the design's in-hospital definition (censored at discharge) is kept as a secondary analysis\"),\n    (\"outcome (design-specified)\", \"in-hospital death, discharged alive censored at discharge\",\n     \"death_28d;followup_days;event_status\", \"secondary\", \"\"),\n    (\"secondary outcomes\", \"90-day, in-hospital and ICU mortality, ICU and hospital LOS\",\n     \"dod;hospital_expire_flag;outtime;los;admittime;dischtime\", \"aligned with published studies\", \"\"),\n    (\"primary method\", \"PS + stabilized IPTW + Cox\", \"pravastatin_exposed\", \"aligned with published studies\",\n     \"1:1 nearest-neighbour PSM (caliper 0.05, no replacement) + pair-clustered Cox as primary; \"\n     \"stabilized IPTW, overlap weights and multivariable Cox models 1-3 as sensitivity analyses\"),\n    (\"severity scores\", \"SAPS II / APS III / LODS used in published studies\", \"sofa_total_24h\", \"deviation\",\n     \"only SOFA available\"),\n    (\"ventilation / RRT\", \"adjusted in some published studies\", \"\", \"deviation\",\n     \"not adjusted: the design treats them as post-exposure interventions\"),\n    (\"competing risk\", \"discharge alive before day 28\", \"event_status\", \"as designed\",\n     \"1=death, 2=discharged alive, 0=administratively censored at 28 d\"),\n    (\"confounders: demographics\", \"age, sex, race, insurance\", \"age;sex;race_group;insurance\", \"as designed\", \"\"),\n    (\"confounders: comorbidity\", \"ICD-based comorbidities\", \"charlson_index;cm_congestive_heart_failure\",\n     \"as designed\", \"\"),\n    (\"confounders: severity\", \"SAPS II or SOFA in first 24 h\", \"sofa_total_24h\", \"deviation\",\n     \"SAPS II not available; SOFA used for adjustment and SOFA tertiles replace SAPS II tertiles\"),\n    (\"confounders: medications\", \"vasopressors, corticosteroids, broad-spectrum antibiotics, insulin (24 h)\",\n     \"med_vasopressor_24h;med_corticosteroid_24h;med_broad_abx_24h;med_insulin_24h\", \"as designed\", \"\"),\n    (\"prior statin\", \"prior statin use (> 7 days before admission) as baseline\", \"prior_statin_use\",\n     \"as designed\", \"\"),\n    (\"unit of analysis\", \"ICU-stay level with robust SE for repeated stays\", \"subject_id;stay_id\", \"deviation\",\n     \"one first qualifying stay per patient; robust (sandwich) SE retained for the weights\"),\n    (\"time zero\", \"follow-up from ICU admission, exposure assessed over 48 h\",\n     \"intime;hours_to_first_pravastatin\", \"caveat\",\n     \"potential immortal time up to 48 h; examined in the 48-hour landmark sensitivity analysis\"),\n    (\"baseline window\", \"covariates from first 24 h\", \"lactate_max;med_vasopressor_24h\", \"caveat\",\n     \"first-24-h measurements may partly follow an early pravastatin dose\"),\n    (\"missing data\", \"multiple imputation by chained equations\", \"lactate_max;weight_kg\", \"as designed\",\n     \"m=20; pf_ratio_min and sofa_respiration (~50% missing) not used\"),\n    (\"data quality\", \"urine output\", \"urine_output_24h_ml\", \"caveat\",\n     \"negative values set to missing before imputation\"),\n]\n\n\ndef main():\n    schema = read_csv(\"schema_validation.csv\")\n    values = read_csv(\"value_validation.csv\")\n    present = set(schema.loc[schema.check == \"column\", \"item\"])\n    rows = []\n    for elem, design, cols, status, note in ELEMENTS:\n        missing = [c for c in cols.split(\";\") if c and c not in present]\n        rows.append({\"element\": elem, \"study_design\": design, \"columns\": cols,\n                     \"columns_available\": not missing, \"missing_columns\": \";\".join(missing),\n                     \"status\": status, \"note\": note})\n    rows.append({\"element\": \"validation\", \"study_design\": \"value checks (step 3)\", \"columns\": \"\",\n                 \"columns_available\": True, \"missing_columns\": \"\",\n                 \"status\": \"pass\" if (values.status == \"pass\").all() else \"fail\",\n                 \"note\": f\"{int((values.status == 'pass').sum())}/{len(values)} rules passed\"})\n    out = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n    write_csv(out, \"protocol_concordance.csv\")\n    log(\"a04\", f\"elements={len(out)} deviations/caveats={int(out.status.isin(['deviation', 'caveat']).sum())}\"\n               f\" unavailable={int((~out.columns_available).sum())}\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n", "outputs": [{"name": "protocol_concordance.csv", "kind": "csv", "exists": true, "bytes": 3415, "rows": 22, "columns": [{"name": "element", "type": ""}, {"name": "study_design", "type": ""}, {"name": "columns", "type": ""}, {"name": "columns_available", "type": ""}, {"name": "missing_columns", "type": ""}, {"name": "status", "type": ""}, {"name": "note", "type": ""}]}]}, {"step": 5, "file": "a05_variable_specification.py", "code": "\"\"\"\nAnalysis step 5. Analysis-variable specification\n\nInput     : protocol_concordance.csv\nOperation : Write the machine-readable specification used by every later step:\n            exposure, outcomes, PS covariates (continuous / binary / categorical with\n            reference levels), transforms, subgroup variables and excluded variables.\nOutput    : analysis_variable_specification.json\n\"\"\"\nfrom common import log, read_csv, write_json\n\nSPEC = {\n    \"exposure\": \"pravastatin_exposed\",\n    \"primary_outcome\": {\"duration\": \"time28_all\", \"event\": \"death28_all\", \"horizon_days\": 28,\n                        \"definition\": \"all-cause death from ICU intime using deathtime, else dod at 12:00; \"\n                                      \"complete follow-up to day 28 (post-discharge deaths included)\"},\n    \"secondary_outcomes\": {\"death90_all\": \"90-day all-cause death (time90_all)\",\n                           \"hosp_death\": \"in-hospital death (hospital_expire_flag)\",\n                           \"icu_death\": \"deathtime <= outtime + 6 h\",\n                           \"icu_los_days\": \"ICU length of stay (los)\",\n                           \"hosp_los_days\": \"hospital length of stay\"},\n    \"design_specified_outcome\": {\"duration\": \"followup_days\", \"event\": \"death_28d\",\n                                 \"note\": \"in-hospital death, discharged alive censored at discharge\"},\n    \"competing_risk_outcome\": {\"variable\": \"event_status\",\n                               \"coding\": {\"1\": \"death\", \"2\": \"discharged alive\", \"0\": \"admin censored at 28 d\"}},\n    \"primary_design\": \"1:1 nearest-neighbour PSM without replacement, caliper 0.05 on PS scale, \"\n                      \"Cox with pair-clustered robust variance (published MIMIC-IV statin-sepsis studies)\",\n    \"ps_covariates\": {\n        \"continuous\": [\"age\", \"charlson_index\", \"sofa_total_24h\", \"hours_admit_to_icu\", \"weight_kg\",\n                       \"heart_rate_max\", \"mbp_min\", \"resp_rate_max\", \"temperature_max\", \"spo2_min\",\n                       \"gcs_min\", \"lactate_max\", \"creatinine_max\", \"platelets_min\", \"wbc_max\",\n                       \"hemoglobin_min\", \"bicarbonate_min\", \"bun_max\", \"glucose_max\",\n                       \"urine_output_24h_ml\"],\n        \"binary\": [\"female\", \"cm_myocardial_infarction\", \"cm_congestive_heart_failure\",\n                   \"cm_peripheral_vascular\", \"cm_cerebrovascular\", \"cm_chronic_pulmonary\", \"cm_renal\",\n                   \"cm_malignancy\", \"cm_metastatic_tumor\", \"cm_severe_liver\", \"cm_hypertension\",\n                   \"cm_dyslipidemia\", \"diabetes_any\", \"prior_statin_use\", \"has_prior_admission\",\n                   \"med_vasopressor_24h\", \"med_corticosteroid_24h\", \"med_broad_abx_24h\",\n                   \"med_insulin_24h\"],\n        \"categorical\": {\"race_group\": \"White\", \"insurance\": \"Medicare\",\n                        \"admission_type_grp\": \"EW EMER.\", \"first_careunit_grp\": \"MICU\",\n                        \"sepsis_category\": \"sepsis\"},\n    },\n    \"transforms\": {\"lactate_max\": \"log\", \"creatinine_max\": \"log\", \"wbc_max\": \"log\", \"bun_max\": \"log\",\n                   \"glucose_max\": \"log\", \"urine_output_24h_ml\": \"log1p\", \"hours_admit_to_icu\": \"log1p\"},\n    \"transformed_names\": {\"lactate_max\": \"log_lactate_max\", \"creatinine_max\": \"log_creatinine_max\",\n                          \"wbc_max\": \"log_wbc_max\", \"bun_max\": \"log_bun_max\",\n                          \"glucose_max\": \"log_glucose_max\",\n                          \"urine_output_24h_ml\": \"log1p_urine_output_24h_ml\",\n                          \"hours_admit_to_icu\": \"log1p_hours_admit_to_icu\"},\n    \"derivations\": {\n        \"female\": \"sex = 'F'\",\n        \"diabetes_any\": \"cm_diabetes_uncomplicated = 1 OR cm_diabetes_complicated = 1\",\n        \"hours_admit_to_icu\": \"negative values set to 0 before log1p\",\n        \"urine_output_24h_ml\": \"negative values set to missing\",\n        \"insurance\": \"missing coded as 'Unknown'\",\n        \"admission_type_grp\": \"EW EMER., URGENT, OBSERVATION ADMIT, else Other\",\n        \"first_careunit_grp\": \"MICU, MICU/SICU, SICU, TSICU, CCU, CVICU, else Other (units with < 50 patients)\",\n    },\n    \"subgroups\": {\"age_group\": [\"<65\", \">=65\"],\n                  \"sex\": [\"F\", \"M\"],\n                  \"sofa_tertile\": \"full-cohort tertiles of sofa_total_24h (substitute for SAPS II tertiles)\",\n                  \"charlson_group\": [\"CCI <3\", \"CCI >=3\"],\n                  \"septic_shock\": \"sepsis_category = 'septic_shock'\",\n                  \"organ_failure_any\": \"n_organ_failures_24h >= 1\"},\n    \"excluded_post_baseline_or_outcome\": [\n        \"los\", \"outtime\", \"last_careunit\", \"dischtime\", \"deathtime\", \"dod\", \"death_time\",\n        \"discharge_location\", \"hospital_expire_flag\", \"admin_end_time\", \"followup_end_time\",\n        \"first_pravastatin_time\", \"hours_to_first_pravastatin\", \"n_pravastatin_orders\",\n        \"n_qualifying_stays\"],\n    \"excluded_high_missingness\": [\"pf_ratio_min\", \"sofa_respiration\"],\n    \"keep_columns\": [\"subject_id\", \"hadm_id\", \"stay_id\", \"intime\", \"pravastatin_exposed\",\n                     \"hours_to_first_pravastatin\", \"death_28d\", \"discharged_alive_before_28d\",\n                     \"event_status\", \"followup_days\", \"sex\", \"n_organ_failures_24h\"],\n}\n\n\ndef main():\n    conc = read_csv(\"protocol_concordance.csv\")\n    if (~conc.columns_available.astype(bool)).any():\n        raise SystemExit(\"protocol_concordance.csv lists unavailable columns\")\n    write_json(SPEC, \"analysis_variable_specification.json\")\n    ps = SPEC[\"ps_covariates\"]\n    log(\"a05\", f\"continuous={len(ps['continuous'])} binary={len(ps['binary'])} \"\n               f\"categorical={len(ps['categorical'])}\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n", "outputs": [{"name": "analysis_variable_specification.json", "kind": "json", "exists": true, "bytes": 4640}]}, {"step": 6, "file": "a06_analysis_cohort.py", "code": "\"\"\"\nAnalysis step 6. Analysis cohort preparation\n\nInput     : cohort_imported.parquet, analysis_variable_specification.json\nOperation : DuckDB SQL derives female, diabetes_any, grouped categories, insurance 'Unknown',\n            cleaned/log-transformed continuous covariates, subgroup variables (age_group,\n            charlson_group, septic_shock, sofa_tertile with full-cohort tertile cut points,\n            organ_failure_any) and outcomes: death28_all/time28_all and death90_all/time90_all\n            (deathtime, else dod at 12:00; post-discharge deaths included), hosp_death, icu_death\n            (deathtime <= outtime + 6 h), icu_los_days, hosp_los_days. No rows are dropped.\nOutput    : analysis_cohort.parquet\n\"\"\"\nfrom common import con_mem, log, read_json, sql_path\n\nSRC = f\"read_parquet('{sql_path('cohort_imported.parquet')}')\"\nOUT_FILE = sql_path(\"analysis_cohort.parquet\")\n\n\ndef build_sql(sp: dict, q1: float, q2: float) -> str:\n    keep = \", \".join(sp[\"keep_columns\"])\n    cont = [c for c in sp[\"ps_covariates\"][\"continuous\"]\n            if c not in (\"hours_admit_to_icu\", \"urine_output_24h_ml\")]\n    binary_src = [c for c in sp[\"ps_covariates\"][\"binary\"] if c not in (\"female\", \"diabetes_any\")]\n    cont_sql = \",\\n    \".join(f\"CAST({c} AS DOUBLE) AS {c}\" for c in cont)\n    bin_sql = \",\\n    \".join(f\"CAST({c} AS INTEGER) AS {c}\" for c in binary_src)\n    log_sql = \",\\n    \".join(f\"ln({c}) AS {sp['transformed_names'][c]}\"\n                             for c, f in sp[\"transforms\"].items() if f == \"log\")\n    return f\"\"\"\nCOPY (\nSELECT\n    {keep},\n    {cont_sql},\n    greatest(hours_admit_to_icu, 0)                                   AS hours_admit_to_icu,\n    CASE WHEN urine_output_24h_ml >= 0 THEN urine_output_24h_ml END  AS urine_output_24h_ml,\n    {bin_sql},\n    CASE WHEN sex = 'F' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END                              AS female,\n    CASE WHEN cm_diabetes_uncomplicated = 1 OR cm_diabetes_complicated = 1\n         THEN 1 ELSE 0 END                                             AS diabetes_any,\n    race_group,\n    coalesce(insurance, 'Unknown')                                     AS insurance,\n    CASE WHEN admission_type IN ('EW EMER.', 'URGENT', 'OBSERVATION ADMIT')\n         THEN admission_type ELSE 'Other' END                          AS admission_type_grp,\n    CASE first_careunit\n         WHEN 'Medical Intensive Care Unit (MICU)'               THEN 'MICU'\n         WHEN 'Medical/Surgical Intensive Care Unit (MICU/SICU)' THEN 'MICU/SICU'\n         WHEN 'Surgical Intensive Care Unit (SICU)'              THEN 'SICU'\n         WHEN 'Trauma SICU (TSICU)'                              THEN 'TSICU'\n         WHEN 'Coronary Care Unit (CCU)'                         THEN 'CCU'\n         WHEN 'Cardiac Vascular Intensive Care Unit (CVICU)'     THEN 'CVICU'\n         ELSE 'Other' END                                              AS first_careunit_grp,\n    sepsis_category,\n    {log_sql},\n    ln(1 + greatest(hours_admit_to_icu, 0))                            AS log1p_hours_admit_to_icu,\n    CASE WHEN urine_output_24h_ml >= 0 THEN ln(1 + urine_output_24h_ml) END\n                                                                       AS log1p_urine_output_24h_ml,\n    CASE WHEN age < 65 THEN '<65' ELSE '>=65' END                      AS age_group,\n    CASE WHEN charlson_index < 3 THEN 'CCI <3' ELSE 'CCI >=3' END      AS charlson_group,\n    CASE WHEN sepsis_category = 'septic_shock' THEN 'septic shock' ELSE 'no septic shock' END\n                                                                       AS septic_shock,\n    -- outcomes (published-study primary: all-cause death incl. post-discharge via dod)\n    CASE WHEN death_time_all <= intime + INTERVAL 28 DAY THEN 1 ELSE 0 END AS death28_all,\n    greatest(date_diff('second', intime, least(coalesce(death_time_all, intime + INTERVAL 28 DAY),\n                                               intime + INTERVAL 28 DAY)) / 86400.0, 0) AS time28_all,\n    CASE WHEN death_time_all <= intime + INTERVAL 90 DAY THEN 1 ELSE 0 END AS death90_all,\n    greatest(date_diff('second', intime, least(coalesce(death_time_all, intime + INTERVAL 90 DAY),\n                                               intime + INTERVAL 90 DAY)) / 86400.0, 0) AS time90_all,\n    CAST(hospital_expire_flag AS INTEGER)                              AS hosp_death,\n    CASE WHEN deathtime IS NOT NULL AND deathtime <= outtime + INTERVAL 6 HOUR THEN 1 ELSE 0 END\n                                                                       AS icu_death,\n    los                                                                AS icu_los_days,\n    date_diff('second', admittime, dischtime) / 86400.0                AS hosp_los_days,\n    CASE WHEN sofa_total_24h <= {q1} THEN 'T1 (SOFA<={q1:g})'\n         WHEN sofa_total_24h <= {q2} THEN 'T2 (SOFA {q1 + 1:g}-{q2:g})'\n         ELSE 'T3 (SOFA>{q2:g})' END                                   AS sofa_tertile,\n    CASE WHEN n_organ_failures_24h >= 1 THEN 'organ failure' ELSE 'no organ failure' END\n                                                                       AS organ_failure_any\nFROM (SELECT *, coalesce(deathtime, CAST(dod AS TIMESTAMP) + INTERVAL 12 HOUR) AS death_time_all\n      FROM {SRC})\nORDER BY subject_id\n) TO '{OUT_FILE}' (FORMAT parquet)\n\"\"\"\n\n\ndef main():\n    sp = read_json(\"analysis_variable_specification.json\")\n    con = con_mem()\n    q1, q2 = con.execute(\n        f\"SELECT quantile_cont(sofa_total_24h, 1/3), quantile_cont(sofa_total_24h, 2/3) FROM {SRC}\").fetchone()\n    con.execute(build_sql(sp, q1, q2))\n    n, n_exp = con.execute(\n        f\"SELECT COUNT(*), SUM(pravastatin_exposed) FROM read_parquet('{OUT_FILE}')\").fetchone()\n    tert = con.execute(f\"SELECT sofa_tertile, COUNT(*) FROM read_parquet('{OUT_FILE}') GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1\").fetchall()\n    chk = con.execute(f\"\"\"SELECT SUM(death28_all), MIN(time28_all), MAX(time28_all),\n                                 SUM(CASE WHEN death28_all = 1 AND death_28d = 0 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END)\n                          FROM read_parquet('{OUT_FILE}')\"\"\").fetchone()\n    log(\"a06\", f\"analysis_cohort rows={n:,} exposed={int(n_exp)} sofa cut points={q1:g},{q2:g} {tert}\")\n    log(\"a06\", f\"death28_all={int(chk[0])} (time {chk[1]:.2f}-{chk[2]:.2f} d); \"\n               f\"post-discharge 28-day deaths added vs design outcome={int(chk[3])}\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n", "outputs": [{"name": "analysis_cohort.parquet", "kind": "parquet", "exists": true, "bytes": 994511, "rows": 9902, "columns": [{"name": "subject_id", "type": "BIGINT"}, {"name": "hadm_id", "type": "BIGINT"}, {"name": "stay_id", "type": "BIGINT"}, {"name": "intime", "type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "pravastatin_exposed", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "hours_to_first_pravastatin", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "death_28d", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "discharged_alive_before_28d", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "event_status", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "followup_days", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "sex", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "n_organ_failures_24h", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "age", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "charlson_index", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "sofa_total_24h", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "weight_kg", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "heart_rate_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "mbp_min", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "resp_rate_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "temperature_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "spo2_min", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "gcs_min", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "lactate_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "creatinine_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "platelets_min", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "wbc_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "hemoglobin_min", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "bicarbonate_min", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "bun_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "glucose_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "hours_admit_to_icu", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "urine_output_24h_ml", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "cm_myocardial_infarction", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_congestive_heart_failure", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_peripheral_vascular", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_cerebrovascular", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_chronic_pulmonary", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_renal", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_malignancy", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_metastatic_tumor", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_severe_liver", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_hypertension", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_dyslipidemia", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "prior_statin_use", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "has_prior_admission", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "med_vasopressor_24h", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "med_corticosteroid_24h", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "med_broad_abx_24h", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "med_insulin_24h", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "female", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "diabetes_any", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "race_group", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "insurance", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "admission_type_grp", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "first_careunit_grp", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "sepsis_category", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "log_lactate_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "log_creatinine_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "log_wbc_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "log_bun_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "log_glucose_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "log1p_hours_admit_to_icu", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "log1p_urine_output_24h_ml", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "age_group", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "charlson_group", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "septic_shock", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "death28_all", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "time28_all", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "death90_all", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "time90_all", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "hosp_death", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "icu_death", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "icu_los_days", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "hosp_los_days", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "sofa_tertile", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "organ_failure_any", "type": "VARCHAR"}]}]}, {"step": 7, "file": "a07_cohort_accounting.py", "code": "\"\"\"\nAnalysis step 7. Cohort accounting and crude outcomes\n\nInput     : analysis_cohort.parquet\nOperation : DuckDB SQL by exposure group and overall: n; 28- and 90-day all-cause deaths\n            (Wilson 95% CI added in Python); in-hospital and ICU deaths; median (IQR) ICU and\n            hospital LOS; design-specified in-hospital 28-day deaths, discharges alive before day\n            28; exposure timing (0-24 h / 24-48 h); deaths before 48 h.\nOutput    : cohort_outcome_counts.csv\n\"\"\"\nimport numpy as np\n\nfrom common import con_mem, log, sql_path, write_csv\n\nSRC = f\"read_parquet('{sql_path('analysis_cohort.parquet')}')\"\n\nSQL = f\"\"\"\nSELECT\n    CASE WHEN GROUPING(pravastatin_exposed) = 1 THEN 'overall'\n         WHEN pravastatin_exposed = 1 THEN 'pravastatin' ELSE 'no pravastatin' END AS grp,\n    COUNT(*)                                                     AS n,\n    SUM(death28_all)                                             AS deaths_28d_all,\n    SUM(death90_all)                                             AS deaths_90d_all,\n    SUM(hosp_death)                                              AS deaths_in_hospital,\n    SUM(icu_death)                                               AS deaths_in_icu,\n    median(icu_los_days)                                         AS icu_los_median,\n    quantile_cont(icu_los_days, 0.25)                            AS icu_los_q1,\n    quantile_cont(icu_los_days, 0.75)                            AS icu_los_q3,\n    median(hosp_los_days)                                        AS hosp_los_median,\n    quantile_cont(hosp_los_days, 0.25)                           AS hosp_los_q1,\n    quantile_cont(hosp_los_days, 0.75)                           AS hosp_los_q3,\n    SUM(death_28d)                                               AS design_deaths_28d_in_hospital,\n    SUM(CASE WHEN event_status = 2 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END)            AS discharged_alive_lt28d,\n    SUM(CASE WHEN hours_to_first_pravastatin <= 24 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS exposed_0_24h,\n    SUM(CASE WHEN hours_to_first_pravastatin > 24 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END)  AS exposed_24_48h,\n    SUM(CASE WHEN time28_all < 2 AND death28_all = 1 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS deaths_before_48h\nFROM {SRC}\nGROUP BY ROLLUP (pravastatin_exposed)\nORDER BY grp\n\"\"\"\n\n\ndef wilson(k, n, z=1.959964):\n    p = k / n\n    den = 1 + z ** 2 / n\n    c = (p + z ** 2 / (2 * n)) / den\n    h = z * np.sqrt(p * (1 - p) / n + z ** 2 / (4 * n ** 2)) / den\n    return c - h, c + h\n\n\ndef main():\n    out = con_mem().execute(SQL).df()\n    for col, lab in ((\"deaths_28d_all\", \"mortality_28d_all\"), (\"deaths_90d_all\", \"mortality_90d_all\")):\n        out[lab] = out[col] / out.n\n        lo, hi = wilson(out[col].astype(float), out.n.astype(float))\n        out[f\"{lab}_ci_low\"], out[f\"{lab}_ci_high\"] = lo, hi\n    write_csv(out, \"cohort_outcome_counts.csv\")\n    for r in out.itertuples():\n        log(\"a07\", f\"{r.grp}: n={r.n} 28d={int(r.deaths_28d_all)} ({r.mortality_28d_all:.1%}) \"\n                   f\"90d={int(r.deaths_90d_all)} ({r.mortality_90d_all:.1%}) in-hosp={int(r.deaths_in_hospital)} \"\n                   f\"ICU={int(r.deaths_in_icu)} design28={int(r.design_deaths_28d_in_hospital)}\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n", "outputs": [{"name": "cohort_outcome_counts.csv", "kind": "csv", "exists": true, "bytes": 1280, "rows": 3, "columns": [{"name": "grp", "type": ""}, {"name": "n", "type": ""}, {"name": "deaths_28d_all", "type": ""}, {"name": "deaths_90d_all", "type": ""}, {"name": "deaths_in_hospital", "type": ""}, {"name": "deaths_in_icu", "type": ""}, {"name": "icu_los_median", "type": ""}, {"name": "icu_los_q1", "type": ""}, {"name": "icu_los_q3", "type": ""}, {"name": "hosp_los_median", "type": ""}, {"name": "hosp_los_q1", "type": ""}, {"name": "hosp_los_q3", "type": ""}, {"name": "design_deaths_28d_in_hospital", "type": ""}, {"name": "discharged_alive_lt28d", "type": ""}, {"name": "exposed_0_24h", "type": ""}, {"name": "exposed_24_48h", "type": ""}, {"name": "deaths_before_48h", "type": ""}, {"name": "mortality_28d_all", "type": ""}, {"name": "mortality_28d_all_ci_low", "type": ""}, {"name": "mortality_28d_all_ci_high", "type": ""}, {"name": "mortality_90d_all", "type": ""}, {"name": "mortality_90d_all_ci_low", "type": ""}, {"name": "mortality_90d_all_ci_high", "type": ""}]}]}, {"step": 8, "file": "a08_missingness.py", "code": "\"\"\"\nAnalysis step 8. Missing-data assessment\n\nInput     : analysis_cohort.parquet, analysis_variable_specification.json\nOperation : DuckDB SQL missing count / % per specified covariate, overall and by exposure.\n            Covariates with > 40% missing are flagged as excluded from imputation.\nOutput    : missingness_summary.csv\n\"\"\"\nimport pandas as pd\n\nfrom common import con_mem, log, model_continuous, read_json, sql_path, write_csv\n\nSRC = f\"read_parquet('{sql_path('analysis_cohort.parquet')}')\"\n\n\ndef main():\n    sp = read_json(\"analysis_variable_specification.json\")\n    ps = sp[\"ps_covariates\"]\n    cols = ps[\"continuous\"] + [c for c in model_continuous(sp) if c not in ps[\"continuous\"]] \\\n        + ps[\"binary\"] + list(ps[\"categorical\"])\n    con = con_mem()\n    rows = []\n    for c in cols:\n        r = con.execute(f\"\"\"\n            SELECT COUNT(*) - COUNT({c}),\n                   COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE pravastatin_exposed = 1 AND {c} IS NULL),\n                   COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE pravastatin_exposed = 0 AND {c} IS NULL),\n                   COUNT(*), SUM(pravastatin_exposed), SUM(1 - pravastatin_exposed)\n            FROM {SRC}\"\"\").fetchone()\n        rows.append({\"variable\": c, \"missing_n\": r[0], \"missing_pct\": 100 * r[0] / r[3],\n                     \"missing_pct_pravastatin\": 100 * r[1] / r[4],\n                     \"missing_pct_no_pravastatin\": 100 * r[2] / r[5],\n                     \"excluded_from_imputation\": 100 * r[0] / r[3] > 40})\n    out = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n    write_csv(out, \"missingness_summary.csv\")\n    top = out[out.missing_n > 0].sort_values(\"missing_pct\", ascending=False).head(6)\n    log(\"a08\", \"highest missingness: \" + \", \".join(f\"{r.variable} {r.missing_pct:.1f}%\" for r in top.itertuples()))\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n", "outputs": [{"name": "missingness_summary.csv", "kind": "csv", "exists": true, "bytes": 2985, "rows": 51, "columns": [{"name": "variable", "type": ""}, {"name": "missing_n", "type": ""}, {"name": "missing_pct", "type": ""}, {"name": "missing_pct_pravastatin", "type": ""}, {"name": "missing_pct_no_pravastatin", "type": ""}, {"name": "excluded_from_imputation", "type": ""}]}]}, {"step": 9, "file": "a09_multiple_imputation.py", "code": "\"\"\"\nAnalysis step 9. Multiple imputation by chained equations\n\nInput     : analysis_cohort.parquet, missingness_summary.csv, analysis_variable_specification.json\nOperation : m=20 imputations, 20 iterations, seeds 20261120+k. Continuous PS covariates are\n            imputed on the transformed scale by Bayesian linear regression draws (equivalent\n            role to sklearn IterativeImputer(BayesianRidge, sample_posterior=True), which is not\n            installed); predictors include exposure, the primary outcome death28_all and the\n            Nelson-Aalen cumulative hazard at time28_all. Exposure and outcome are never imputed. Long format with 'imputation'.\nOutput    : imputed_cohorts.parquet (+ imputation_summary.csv)\n\"\"\"\nimport time\n\nimport pandas as pd\n\nfrom common import log, mice, model_continuous, read_csv, read_json, read_parquet, write_csv, write_parquet\n\n\ndef main():\n    t0 = time.time()\n    sp = read_json(\"analysis_variable_specification.json\")\n    miss = read_csv(\"missingness_summary.csv\")\n    too_missing = set(miss.loc[miss.excluded_from_imputation, \"variable\"])\n    bad = too_missing & set(model_continuous(sp) + sp[\"ps_covariates\"][\"continuous\"])\n    if bad:\n        raise SystemExit(f\"covariates over 40% missing are in the PS model: {sorted(bad)}\")\n    df = read_parquet(\"analysis_cohort.parquet\")\n    imp = mice(df, sp)\n    write_parquet(imp, \"imputed_cohorts.parquet\")\n\n    rows = []\n    for c in model_continuous(sp):\n        obs = df[c].dropna()\n        mis_mask = df[c].isna().to_numpy()\n        imputed_vals = pd.concat([g.loc[mis_mask, c] for _, g in imp.groupby(\"imputation\")]) \\\n            if mis_mask.any() else pd.Series(dtype=float)\n        rows.append({\"variable\": c, \"n_missing\": int(mis_mask.sum()), \"observed_mean\": obs.mean(),\n                     \"observed_sd\": obs.std(), \"imputed_mean\": imputed_vals.mean(),\n                     \"imputed_sd\": imputed_vals.std()})\n    write_csv(pd.DataFrame(rows), \"imputation_summary.csv\")\n    assert imp[model_continuous(sp)].isna().sum().sum() == 0\n    log(\"a09\", f\"imputed_cohorts rows={len(imp):,} (m={imp.imputation.nunique()}) ({time.time() - t0:.1f}s)\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n", "outputs": [{"name": "imputed_cohorts.parquet", "kind": "parquet", "exists": true, "bytes": 13412523, "rows": 198040, "columns": [{"name": "imputation", "type": "BIGINT"}, {"name": "subject_id", "type": "BIGINT"}, {"name": "hadm_id", "type": "BIGINT"}, {"name": "stay_id", "type": "BIGINT"}, {"name": "intime", "type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "pravastatin_exposed", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "hours_to_first_pravastatin", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "death_28d", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "discharged_alive_before_28d", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "event_status", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "followup_days", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "sex", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "n_organ_failures_24h", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "age", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "charlson_index", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "sofa_total_24h", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "weight_kg", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "heart_rate_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "mbp_min", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "resp_rate_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "temperature_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "spo2_min", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "gcs_min", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "lactate_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "creatinine_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "platelets_min", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "wbc_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "hemoglobin_min", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "bicarbonate_min", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "bun_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "glucose_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "hours_admit_to_icu", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "urine_output_24h_ml", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "cm_myocardial_infarction", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_congestive_heart_failure", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_peripheral_vascular", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_cerebrovascular", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_chronic_pulmonary", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_renal", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_malignancy", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_metastatic_tumor", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_severe_liver", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_hypertension", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_dyslipidemia", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "prior_statin_use", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "has_prior_admission", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "med_vasopressor_24h", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "med_corticosteroid_24h", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "med_broad_abx_24h", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "med_insulin_24h", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "female", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "diabetes_any", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "race_group", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "insurance", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "admission_type_grp", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "first_careunit_grp", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "sepsis_category", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "log_lactate_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "log_creatinine_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "log_wbc_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "log_bun_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "log_glucose_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "log1p_hours_admit_to_icu", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "log1p_urine_output_24h_ml", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "age_group", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "charlson_group", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "septic_shock", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "death28_all", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "time28_all", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "death90_all", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "time90_all", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "hosp_death", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "icu_death", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "icu_los_days", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "hosp_los_days", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "sofa_tertile", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "organ_failure_any", "type": "VARCHAR"}]}, {"name": "imputation_summary.csv", "kind": "csv", "exists": true, "bytes": 1780, "rows": 20, "columns": [{"name": "variable", "type": ""}, {"name": "n_missing", "type": ""}, {"name": "observed_mean", "type": ""}, {"name": "observed_sd", "type": ""}, {"name": "imputed_mean", "type": ""}, {"name": "imputed_sd", "type": ""}]}]}, {"step": 10, "file": "a10_baseline_unweighted.py", "code": "\"\"\"\nAnalysis step 10. Unweighted baseline summary and standardized mean differences\n\nInput     : analysis_cohort.parquet (observed, non-imputed data)\nOperation : By exposure group: mean, SD, median, IQR and missing n for continuous covariates\n            (original scale); n (%) for binary covariates and categorical levels. Absolute SMD\n            with pooled SD sqrt((var1 + var0) / 2).\nOutput    : baseline_unweighted.csv\n\"\"\"\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\nfrom common import EXPOSURE, log, read_json, read_parquet, smd, write_csv\n\n\ndef main():\n    sp = read_json(\"analysis_variable_specification.json\")\n    df = read_parquet(\"analysis_cohort.parquet\")\n    a = df[EXPOSURE].to_numpy()\n    rows = []\n    for c in sp[\"ps_covariates\"][\"continuous\"]:\n        x = df[c].astype(float).to_numpy()\n        r = {\"variable\": c, \"level\": \"\", \"type\": \"continuous\"}\n        for g, lab in ((1, \"pravastatin\"), (0, \"no_pravastatin\")):\n            v = x[(a == g) & ~np.isnan(x)]\n            r.update({f\"{lab}_n\": len(v), f\"{lab}_mean\": v.mean(), f\"{lab}_sd\": v.std(ddof=1),\n                      f\"{lab}_median\": np.median(v), f\"{lab}_q1\": np.percentile(v, 25),\n                      f\"{lab}_q3\": np.percentile(v, 75), f\"{lab}_missing\": int(np.isnan(x[a == g]).sum())})\n        r[\"smd_unweighted\"] = smd(x, a)\n        rows.append(r)\n    indicators = [(c, \"1\", df[c].astype(float).to_numpy()) for c in sp[\"ps_covariates\"][\"binary\"]]\n    for c in sp[\"ps_covariates\"][\"categorical\"]:\n        for lev in sorted(df[c].dropna().unique()):\n            indicators.append((c, lev, (df[c] == lev).astype(float).to_numpy()))\n    for c, lev, x in indicators:\n        r = {\"variable\": c, \"level\": lev, \"type\": \"binary\" if lev == \"1\" else \"categorical\"}\n        for g, lab in ((1, \"pravastatin\"), (0, \"no_pravastatin\")):\n            v = x[a == g]\n            r.update({f\"{lab}_n\": int(v.sum()), f\"{lab}_pct\": 100 * v.mean()})\n        r[\"smd_unweighted\"] = smd(x, a)\n        rows.append(r)\n    out = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n    write_csv(out, \"baseline_unweighted.csv\")\n    top = out.sort_values(\"smd_unweighted\", ascending=False).head(5)\n    log(\"a10\", f\"rows={len(out)}; largest SMD: \" +\n        \", \".join(f\"{r.variable}{'=' + r.level if r.level not in ('', '1') else ''} {r.smd_unweighted:.2f}\"\n                  for r in top.itertuples()))\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n", "outputs": [{"name": "baseline_unweighted.csv", "kind": "csv", "exists": true, "bytes": 8617, "rows": 64, "columns": [{"name": "variable", "type": ""}, {"name": "level", "type": ""}, {"name": "type", "type": ""}, {"name": "pravastatin_n", "type": ""}, {"name": "pravastatin_mean", "type": ""}, {"name": "pravastatin_sd", "type": ""}, {"name": "pravastatin_median", "type": ""}, {"name": "pravastatin_q1", "type": ""}, {"name": "pravastatin_q3", "type": ""}, {"name": "pravastatin_missing", "type": ""}, {"name": "no_pravastatin_n", "type": ""}, {"name": "no_pravastatin_mean", "type": ""}, {"name": "no_pravastatin_sd", "type": ""}, {"name": "no_pravastatin_median", "type": ""}, {"name": "no_pravastatin_q1", "type": ""}, {"name": "no_pravastatin_q3", "type": ""}, {"name": "no_pravastatin_missing", "type": ""}, {"name": "smd_unweighted", "type": ""}, {"name": "pravastatin_pct", "type": ""}, {"name": "no_pravastatin_pct", "type": ""}]}]}, {"step": 11, "file": "a11_propensity_scores.py", "code": "\"\"\"\nAnalysis step 11. Propensity-score estimation\n\nInput     : imputed_cohorts.parquet, analysis_variable_specification.json\nOperation : Within each imputation, unpenalized multivariable logistic regression (IRLS) of\n            pravastatin_exposed on all PS covariates (z-scored continuous, binaries, one-hot\n            categories with reference levels). Records convergence, separation and C-statistic.\n            If ANY imputation fails to converge or separates, ALL imputations are refit with\n            L2-penalized logistic regression (C=1.0) as prespecified.\nOutput    : propensity_scores.parquet (+ propensity_model_diagnostics.csv)\n\"\"\"\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\nfrom common import EXPOSURE, c_statistic, design_matrix, fit_logistic, log, read_json, read_parquet, \\\n    write_csv, write_parquet\n\n\ndef fit_all(imp, sp, l2):\n    scores, diags = [], []\n    for k, d in imp.groupby(\"imputation\", sort=True):\n        X, names = design_matrix(d, sp)\n        y = d[EXPOSURE].to_numpy().astype(float)\n        f = fit_logistic(X, y, l2=l2)\n        scores.append(pd.DataFrame({\"subject_id\": d.subject_id.to_numpy(), \"imputation\": k, \"ps\": f[\"p\"]}))\n        diags.append({\"imputation\": k, \"n_params\": X.shape[1] + 1, \"converged\": f[\"converged\"],\n                      \"iterations\": f[\"iterations\"], \"separation\": f[\"separation\"],\n                      \"c_statistic\": c_statistic(y, f[\"p\"]), \"max_abs_coef\": float(np.max(np.abs(f[\"beta\"][1:])))})\n    return pd.concat(scores, ignore_index=True), pd.DataFrame(diags)\n\n\ndef main():\n    sp = read_json(\"analysis_variable_specification.json\")\n    imp = read_parquet(\"imputed_cohorts.parquet\")\n    scores, diag = fit_all(imp, sp, l2=0.0)\n    method = \"unpenalized_logit\"\n    if (~diag.converged).any() or diag.separation.any():\n        scores, diag = fit_all(imp, sp, l2=1.0)\n        method = \"ridge_logit_C1_fallback\"\n    diag[\"method\"] = method\n    write_parquet(scores, \"propensity_scores.parquet\")\n    write_csv(diag, \"propensity_model_diagnostics.csv\")\n    log(\"a11\", f\"method={method} params={diag.n_params.iloc[0]} \"\n               f\"C-statistic mean={diag.c_statistic.mean():.3f} \"\n               f\"(range {diag.c_statistic.min():.3f}-{diag.c_statistic.max():.3f})\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n", "outputs": [{"name": "propensity_scores.parquet", "kind": "parquet", "exists": true, "bytes": 2063073, "rows": 198040, "columns": [{"name": "subject_id", "type": "BIGINT"}, {"name": "imputation", "type": "BIGINT"}, {"name": "ps", "type": "DOUBLE"}]}, {"name": "propensity_model_diagnostics.csv", "kind": "csv", "exists": true, "bytes": 1728, "rows": 20, "columns": [{"name": "imputation", "type": ""}, {"name": "n_params", "type": ""}, {"name": "converged", "type": ""}, {"name": "iterations", "type": ""}, {"name": "separation", "type": ""}, {"name": "c_statistic", "type": ""}, {"name": "max_abs_coef", "type": ""}, {"name": "method", "type": ""}]}]}, {"step": 12, "file": "a12_ps_overlap.py", "code": "\"\"\"\nAnalysis step 12. Propensity-score overlap assessment\n\nInput     : propensity_scores.parquet, imputed_cohorts.parquet (exposure only)\nOperation : DuckDB SQL per imputation and exposure group: min, 1/5/50/95/99th percentiles,\n            max, and n outside the other group's range; histogram bin counts (20 bins on 0-1)\n            for imputation 1.\nOutput    : propensity_overlap.csv (+ propensity_histogram_imp1.csv)\n\"\"\"\nfrom common import con_mem, log, sql_path, write_csv\n\nPS = f\"read_parquet('{sql_path('propensity_scores.parquet')}')\"\nIMP = f\"read_parquet('{sql_path('imputed_cohorts.parquet')}')\"\n\nBASE = f\"\"\"\nWITH s AS (\n    SELECT p.imputation, p.subject_id, p.ps, i.pravastatin_exposed AS a\n    FROM {PS} p JOIN {IMP} i USING (imputation, subject_id)\n)\n\"\"\"\n\nSUMMARY_SQL = BASE + \"\"\",\nrng AS (SELECT imputation, a, min(ps) AS lo, max(ps) AS hi FROM s GROUP BY ALL)\nSELECT s.imputation,\n       CASE WHEN s.a = 1 THEN 'pravastatin' ELSE 'no_pravastatin' END AS grp,\n       COUNT(*) AS n, min(ps) AS ps_min,\n       quantile_cont(ps, 0.01) AS ps_p01, quantile_cont(ps, 0.05) AS ps_p05,\n       quantile_cont(ps, 0.50) AS ps_p50, quantile_cont(ps, 0.95) AS ps_p95,\n       quantile_cont(ps, 0.99) AS ps_p99, max(ps) AS ps_max,\n       COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE ps < o.lo OR ps > o.hi) AS n_outside_other_group_range\nFROM s JOIN rng o ON o.imputation = s.imputation AND o.a <> s.a\nGROUP BY ALL ORDER BY 1, 2\n\"\"\"\n\nHIST_SQL = BASE + \"\"\"\nSELECT CASE WHEN a = 1 THEN 'pravastatin' ELSE 'no_pravastatin' END AS grp,\n       least(floor(ps * 20), 19) / 20 AS bin_lower, COUNT(*) AS n\nFROM s WHERE imputation = 1 GROUP BY ALL ORDER BY 1, 2\n\"\"\"\n\n\ndef main():\n    con = con_mem()\n    out = con.execute(SUMMARY_SQL).df()\n    write_csv(out, \"propensity_overlap.csv\")\n    write_csv(con.execute(HIST_SQL).df(), \"propensity_histogram_imp1.csv\")\n    m = out.groupby(\"grp\")[[\"ps_p50\", \"ps_max\", \"n_outside_other_group_range\"]].mean()\n    log(\"a12\", \"mean over imputations: \" + \"; \".join(\n        f\"{g}: median PS {r.ps_p50:.3f}, max {r.ps_max:.3f}, outside {r.n_outside_other_group_range:.1f}\"\n        for g, r in m.iterrows()))\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n", "outputs": [{"name": "propensity_overlap.csv", "kind": "csv", "exists": true, "bytes": 6836, "rows": 40, "columns": [{"name": "imputation", "type": ""}, {"name": "grp", "type": ""}, {"name": "n", "type": ""}, {"name": "ps_min", "type": ""}, {"name": "ps_p01", "type": ""}, {"name": "ps_p05", "type": ""}, {"name": "ps_p50", "type": ""}, {"name": "ps_p95", "type": ""}, {"name": "ps_p99", "type": ""}, {"name": "ps_max", "type": ""}, {"name": "n_outside_other_group_range", "type": ""}]}, {"name": "propensity_histogram_imp1.csv", "kind": "csv", "exists": true, "bytes": 416, "rows": 18, "columns": [{"name": "grp", "type": ""}, {"name": "bin_lower", "type": ""}, {"name": "n", "type": ""}]}]}, {"step": 13, "file": "a13_ps_matching.py", "code": "\"\"\"\nAnalysis step 13. 1:1 nearest-neighbour propensity-score matching (primary design)\n\nInput     : propensity_scores.parquet, imputed_cohorts.parquet\nOperation : Within each imputation, greedy 1:1 nearest-neighbour matching on the PS without\n            replacement, exposed processed in descending PS order, caliper 0.05 on the PS\n            scale (as in the published MIMIC-IV statin-sepsis cohorts). pair_id per pair.\nOutput    : matched_cohorts.parquet (+ matching_summary.csv)\n\"\"\"\nimport pandas as pd\n\nfrom common import CALIPER_PS, EXPOSURE, log, matched_frame, read_parquet, write_csv, write_parquet\n\n\ndef main():\n    imp = read_parquet(\"imputed_cohorts.parquet\")\n    ps = read_parquet(\"propensity_scores.parquet\")\n    df = imp.merge(ps, on=[\"imputation\", \"subject_id\"], how=\"inner\", validate=\"one_to_one\")\n    out, summ = [], []\n    for k, d in df.groupby(\"imputation\"):\n        d = d.reset_index(drop=True)\n        m = matched_frame(d.drop(columns=\"ps\"), d[\"ps\"].to_numpy(), CALIPER_PS, \"ps\")\n        out.append(m)\n        n_exp = int(d[EXPOSURE].sum())\n        summ.append({\"imputation\": k, \"exposed_total\": n_exp, \"matched_pairs\": int(m.pair_id.nunique()),\n                     \"unmatched_exposed\": n_exp - int(m.pair_id.nunique()), \"caliper_ps\": CALIPER_PS})\n    out = pd.concat(out, ignore_index=True)\n    write_parquet(out, \"matched_cohorts.parquet\")\n    s = pd.DataFrame(summ)\n    write_csv(s, \"matching_summary.csv\")\n    log(\"a13\", f\"matched pairs per imputation {s.matched_pairs.min()}-{s.matched_pairs.max()} \"\n               f\"of {s.exposed_total.iloc[0]} exposed (caliper {CALIPER_PS} on PS scale)\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n", "outputs": [{"name": "matched_cohorts.parquet", "kind": "parquet", "exists": true, "bytes": 976511, "rows": 10074, "columns": [{"name": "imputation", "type": "BIGINT"}, {"name": "subject_id", "type": "BIGINT"}, {"name": "hadm_id", "type": "BIGINT"}, {"name": "stay_id", "type": "BIGINT"}, {"name": "intime", "type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "pravastatin_exposed", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "hours_to_first_pravastatin", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "death_28d", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "discharged_alive_before_28d", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "event_status", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "followup_days", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "sex", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "n_organ_failures_24h", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "age", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "charlson_index", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "sofa_total_24h", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "weight_kg", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "heart_rate_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "mbp_min", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "resp_rate_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "temperature_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "spo2_min", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "gcs_min", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "lactate_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "creatinine_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "platelets_min", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "wbc_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "hemoglobin_min", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "bicarbonate_min", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "bun_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "glucose_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "hours_admit_to_icu", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "urine_output_24h_ml", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "cm_myocardial_infarction", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_congestive_heart_failure", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_peripheral_vascular", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_cerebrovascular", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_chronic_pulmonary", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_renal", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_malignancy", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_metastatic_tumor", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_severe_liver", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_hypertension", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_dyslipidemia", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "prior_statin_use", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "has_prior_admission", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "med_vasopressor_24h", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "med_corticosteroid_24h", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "med_broad_abx_24h", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "med_insulin_24h", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "female", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "diabetes_any", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "race_group", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "insurance", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "admission_type_grp", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "first_careunit_grp", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "sepsis_category", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "log_lactate_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "log_creatinine_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "log_wbc_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "log_bun_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "log_glucose_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "log1p_hours_admit_to_icu", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "log1p_urine_output_24h_ml", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "age_group", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "charlson_group", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "septic_shock", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "death28_all", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "time28_all", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "death90_all", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "time90_all", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "hosp_death", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "icu_death", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "icu_los_days", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "hosp_los_days", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "sofa_tertile", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "organ_failure_any", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "pair_id", "type": "BIGINT"}, {"name": "ps", "type": "DOUBLE"}]}, {"name": "matching_summary.csv", "kind": "csv", "exists": true, "bytes": 440, "rows": 20, "columns": [{"name": "imputation", "type": ""}, {"name": "exposed_total", "type": ""}, {"name": "matched_pairs", "type": ""}, {"name": "unmatched_exposed", "type": ""}, {"name": "caliper_ps", "type": ""}]}]}, {"step": 14, "file": "a14_matched_balance.py", "code": "\"\"\"\nAnalysis step 14. Matched-cohort balance assessment\n\nInput     : matched_cohorts.parquet, matching_summary.csv\nOperation : Per imputation, absolute SMD of every covariate / categorical level in the matched\n            cohort (pooled SD of the matched groups) and matched-group means; averaged across\n            imputations; balanced if averaged SMD < 0.10.\nOutput    : matched_balance.csv\n\"\"\"\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\nfrom common import EXPOSURE, balance_columns, log, read_csv, read_json, read_parquet, smd, write_csv\n\n\ndef main():\n    sp = read_json(\"analysis_variable_specification.json\")\n    m = read_parquet(\"matched_cohorts.parquet\")\n    rows = []\n    for k, d in m.groupby(\"imputation\"):\n        a = d[EXPOSURE].to_numpy()\n        for name, x in balance_columns(d, sp).items():\n            rows.append({\"imputation\": k, \"covariate\": name, \"mean_pravastatin\": x[a == 1].mean(),\n                         \"mean_no_pravastatin\": x[a == 0].mean(), \"smd_matched\": smd(x, a)})\n    per = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n    out = per.groupby(\"covariate\", sort=False).mean(numeric_only=True).drop(columns=\"imputation\").reset_index()\n    out[\"smd_matched_max_over_imputations\"] = per.groupby(\"covariate\", sort=False)[\"smd_matched\"].max().to_numpy()\n    out[\"balanced\"] = out.smd_matched < 0.10\n    write_csv(out, \"matched_balance.csv\")\n    s = read_csv(\"matching_summary.csv\")\n    worst = out.sort_values(\"smd_matched\", ascending=False).iloc[0]\n    log(\"a14\", f\"pairs={s.matched_pairs.mean():.0f}; imbalanced={int((~out.balanced).sum())}/{len(out)}; \"\n               f\"max averaged SMD={worst.smd_matched:.3f} ({worst.covariate})\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n", "outputs": [{"name": "matched_balance.csv", "kind": "csv", "exists": true, "bytes": 6678, "rows": 64, "columns": [{"name": "covariate", "type": ""}, {"name": "mean_pravastatin", "type": ""}, {"name": "mean_no_pravastatin", "type": ""}, {"name": "smd_matched", "type": ""}, {"name": "smd_matched_max_over_imputations", "type": ""}, {"name": "balanced", "type": ""}]}]}, {"step": 15, "file": "a15_iptw.py", "code": "\"\"\"\nAnalysis step 15. Stabilized IPTW construction (sensitivity design)\n\nInput     : propensity_scores.parquet, imputed_cohorts.parquet\nOperation : Within each imputation: stabilized ATE weights p/PS (exposed), (1-p)/(1-PS)\n            (unexposed) -> sw_raw; truncated at the 1st/99th percentiles within each exposure\n            group -> sw; overlap weights (1-PS exposed, PS unexposed) -> ow.\nOutput    : iptw_cohort.parquet\n\"\"\"\nimport numpy as np\n\nfrom common import EXPOSURE, alternative_weights, log, read_parquet, stabilized_weights, write_parquet\n\n\ndef main():\n    imp = read_parquet(\"imputed_cohorts.parquet\")\n    ps = read_parquet(\"propensity_scores.parquet\")\n    df = imp.merge(ps, on=[\"imputation\", \"subject_id\"], how=\"inner\", validate=\"one_to_one\")\n    df[\"sw_raw\"] = np.nan\n    df[\"sw\"] = np.nan\n    df[\"ow\"] = np.nan\n    for _, idx in df.groupby(\"imputation\").groups.items():\n        a = df.loc[idx, EXPOSURE].to_numpy()\n        p = df.loc[idx, \"ps\"].to_numpy()\n        raw, sw = stabilized_weights(a, p)\n        df.loc[idx, \"sw_raw\"] = raw\n        df.loc[idx, \"sw\"] = sw\n        df.loc[idx, \"ow\"] = alternative_weights(a, p, \"overlap\")\n    write_parquet(df, \"iptw_cohort.parquet\")\n    log(\"a15\", f\"rows={len(df):,} sw range={df.sw.min():.3f}-{df.sw.max():.3f} sw_raw max={df.sw_raw.max():.2f}\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n", "outputs": [{"name": "iptw_cohort.parquet", "kind": "parquet", "exists": true, "bytes": 19750991, "rows": 198040, "columns": [{"name": "imputation", "type": "BIGINT"}, {"name": "subject_id", "type": "BIGINT"}, {"name": "hadm_id", "type": "BIGINT"}, {"name": "stay_id", "type": "BIGINT"}, {"name": "intime", "type": "TIMESTAMP"}, {"name": "pravastatin_exposed", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "hours_to_first_pravastatin", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "death_28d", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "discharged_alive_before_28d", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "event_status", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "followup_days", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "sex", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "n_organ_failures_24h", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "age", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "charlson_index", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "sofa_total_24h", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "weight_kg", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "heart_rate_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "mbp_min", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "resp_rate_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "temperature_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "spo2_min", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "gcs_min", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "lactate_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "creatinine_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "platelets_min", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "wbc_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "hemoglobin_min", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "bicarbonate_min", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "bun_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "glucose_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "hours_admit_to_icu", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "urine_output_24h_ml", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "cm_myocardial_infarction", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_congestive_heart_failure", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_peripheral_vascular", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_cerebrovascular", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_chronic_pulmonary", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_renal", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_malignancy", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_metastatic_tumor", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_severe_liver", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_hypertension", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "cm_dyslipidemia", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "prior_statin_use", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "has_prior_admission", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "med_vasopressor_24h", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "med_corticosteroid_24h", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "med_broad_abx_24h", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "med_insulin_24h", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "female", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "diabetes_any", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "race_group", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "insurance", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "admission_type_grp", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "first_careunit_grp", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "sepsis_category", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "log_lactate_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "log_creatinine_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "log_wbc_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "log_bun_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "log_glucose_max", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "log1p_hours_admit_to_icu", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "log1p_urine_output_24h_ml", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "age_group", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "charlson_group", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "septic_shock", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "death28_all", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "time28_all", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "death90_all", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "time90_all", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "hosp_death", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "icu_death", "type": "INTEGER"}, {"name": "icu_los_days", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "hosp_los_days", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "sofa_tertile", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "organ_failure_any", "type": "VARCHAR"}, {"name": "ps", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "sw_raw", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "sw", "type": "DOUBLE"}, {"name": "ow", "type": "DOUBLE"}]}]}, {"step": 16, "file": "a16_weight_balance.py", "code": "\"\"\"\nAnalysis step 16. Weight diagnostics and weighted balance\n\nInput     : iptw_cohort.parquet\nOperation : DuckDB SQL weight summaries (count, sum, mean, SD, min, 1/50/99th pct, max, ESS)\n            per imputation x group x weight (sw, sw_raw, ow). Weighted SMDs for sw and ow per\n            imputation (unweighted pooled SD as denominator), averaged over imputations.\nOutput    : iptw_diagnostics.csv, weighted_balance.csv\n\"\"\"\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\nfrom common import EXPOSURE, balance_columns, con_mem, log, read_json, read_parquet, smd, sql_path, write_csv\n\nSRC = f\"read_parquet('{sql_path('iptw_cohort.parquet')}')\"\n\n\ndef weight_sql(col: str) -> str:\n    return f\"\"\"\n    SELECT imputation, '{col}' AS weight,\n           CASE WHEN pravastatin_exposed = 1 THEN 'pravastatin' ELSE 'no_pravastatin' END AS grp,\n           COUNT(*) AS n, SUM({col}) AS w_sum, AVG({col}) AS w_mean, stddev_samp({col}) AS w_sd,\n           min({col}) AS w_min, quantile_cont({col}, 0.01) AS w_p01, quantile_cont({col}, 0.5) AS w_p50,\n           quantile_cont({col}, 0.99) AS w_p99, max({col}) AS w_max,\n           SUM({col}) * SUM({col}) / SUM({col} * {col}) AS ess\n    FROM {SRC} GROUP BY ALL\"\"\"\n\n\ndef main():\n    diag = con_mem().execute(\n        \" UNION ALL \".join(weight_sql(c) for c in (\"sw\", \"sw_raw\", \"ow\")) + \" ORDER BY weight, imputation, grp\").df()\n    write_csv(diag, \"iptw_diagnostics.csv\")\n\n    sp = read_json(\"analysis_variable_specification.json\")\n    df = read_parquet(\"iptw_cohort.parquet\")\n    rows = []\n    for k, d in df.groupby(\"imputation\"):\n        a = d[EXPOSURE].to_numpy()\n        for name, x in balance_columns(d, sp).items():\n            sd = np.sqrt((x[a == 1].var(ddof=1) + x[a == 0].var(ddof=1)) / 2)\n            rows.append({\"imputation\": k, \"covariate\": name,\n                         \"smd_unweighted_imputed\": smd(x, a, None, sd),\n                         \"smd_iptw\": smd(x, a, d[\"sw\"].to_numpy(), sd),\n                         \"smd_overlap\": smd(x, a, d[\"ow\"].to_numpy(), sd)})\n    out = pd.DataFrame(rows).groupby(\"covariate\", sort=False).mean(numeric_only=True) \\\n        .drop(columns=\"imputation\").reset_index()\n    out[\"balanced_iptw\"] = out.smd_iptw < 0.10\n    out[\"balanced_overlap\"] = out.smd_overlap < 0.10\n    write_csv(out, \"weighted_balance.csv\")\n    ess = diag[(diag.weight == \"sw\") & (diag.grp == \"pravastatin\")].ess.mean()\n    log(\"a16\", f\"IPTW max SMD={out.smd_iptw.max():.3f} (imbalanced {int((~out.balanced_iptw).sum())}); \"\n               f\"overlap max SMD={out.smd_overlap.max():.3f}; exposed ESS (sw)={ess:.0f}\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n", "outputs": [{"name": "iptw_diagnostics.csv", "kind": "csv", "exists": true, "bytes": 23755, "rows": 120, "columns": [{"name": "imputation", "type": ""}, {"name": "weight", "type": ""}, {"name": "grp", "type": ""}, {"name": "n", "type": ""}, {"name": "w_sum", "type": ""}, {"name": "w_mean", "type": ""}, {"name": "w_sd", "type": ""}, {"name": "w_min", "type": ""}, {"name": "w_p01", "type": ""}, {"name": "w_p50", "type": ""}, {"name": "w_p99", "type": ""}, {"name": "w_max", "type": ""}, {"name": "ess", "type": ""}]}, {"name": "weighted_balance.csv", "kind": "csv", "exists": true, "bytes": 5886, "rows": 64, "columns": [{"name": "covariate", "type": ""}, {"name": "smd_unweighted_imputed", "type": ""}, {"name": "smd_iptw", "type": ""}, {"name": "smd_overlap", "type": ""}, {"name": "balanced_iptw", "type": ""}, {"name": "balanced_overlap", "type": ""}]}]}, {"step": 17, "file": "a17_table1.py", "code": "\"\"\"\nAnalysis step 17. Publication-style Table 1 construction\n\nInput     : baseline_unweighted.csv, matched_cohorts.parquet, matched_balance.csv, weighted_balance.csv\nOperation : Per covariate / level: full-cohort summaries by group and SMD, matched-cohort summaries\n            (imputation 1 matched set) and SMD averaged over imputations, plus IPTW SMD.\n            Continuous: mean (SD); binary/categorical: n (%).\nOutput    : table1_baseline_characteristics.csv\n\"\"\"\nimport pandas as pd\n\nfrom common import EXPOSURE, log, read_csv, read_json, read_parquet, write_csv\n\n\ndef fmt_cont(x):\n    return f\"{x.mean():.1f} ({x.std(ddof=1):.1f})\"\n\n\ndef fmt_bin(x):\n    return f\"{int(x.sum())} ({100 * x.mean():.1f}%)\"\n\n\ndef main():\n    sp = read_json(\"analysis_variable_specification.json\")\n    base = read_csv(\"baseline_unweighted.csv\")\n    mbal = read_csv(\"matched_balance.csv\").set_index(\"covariate\")\n    wbal = read_csv(\"weighted_balance.csv\").set_index(\"covariate\")\n    m1 = read_parquet(\"matched_cohorts.parquet\")\n    m1 = m1[m1.imputation == 1]\n    e, u = m1[m1[EXPOSURE] == 1], m1[m1[EXPOSURE] == 0]\n    n_full_e = int(base.pravastatin_n.iloc[0] + base.pravastatin_missing.iloc[0])\n    n_full_u = int(base.no_pravastatin_n.iloc[0] + base.no_pravastatin_missing.iloc[0])\n    rows = [{\"variable\": \"N\", \"level\": \"\", \"full_pravastatin\": n_full_e, \"full_no_pravastatin\": n_full_u,\n             \"smd_full\": \"\", \"matched_pravastatin\": len(e), \"matched_no_pravastatin\": len(u),\n             \"smd_matched\": \"\", \"smd_iptw\": \"\"}]\n    for r in base.itertuples():\n        if r.type == \"continuous\":\n            key, lev, label = r.variable, \"\", f\"{r.variable}, mean (SD)\"\n            fe = f\"{r.pravastatin_mean:.1f} ({r.pravastatin_sd:.1f})\"\n            fu = f\"{r.no_pravastatin_mean:.1f} ({r.no_pravastatin_sd:.1f})\"\n            me, mu = fmt_cont(e[r.variable]), fmt_cont(u[r.variable])\n        else:\n            if r.type == \"binary\":\n                key, lev = r.variable, \"\"\n                xe, xu = e[r.variable].astype(float), u[r.variable].astype(float)\n            else:\n                key, lev = f\"{r.variable}={r.level}\", r.level\n                xe, xu = (e[r.variable] == r.level).astype(float), (u[r.variable] == r.level).astype(float)\n            label = f\"{r.variable}, n (%)\"\n            fe = f\"{int(r.pravastatin_n)} ({r.pravastatin_pct:.1f}%)\"\n            fu = f\"{int(r.no_pravastatin_n)} ({r.no_pravastatin_pct:.1f}%)\"\n            me, mu = fmt_bin(xe), fmt_bin(xu)\n        rows.append({\"variable\": label, \"level\": lev, \"full_pravastatin\": fe, \"full_no_pravastatin\": fu,\n                     \"smd_full\": round(r.smd_unweighted, 3), \"matched_pravastatin\": me,\n                     \"matched_no_pravastatin\": mu, \"smd_matched\": round(mbal.loc[key, \"smd_matched\"], 3),\n                     \"smd_iptw\": round(wbal.loc[key, \"smd_iptw\"], 3)})\n    out = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n    write_csv(out, \"table1_baseline_characteristics.csv\")\n    log(\"a17\", f\"Table 1 rows={len(out)}; matched n={len(e)}+{len(u)} (imputation 1)\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n", "outputs": [{"name": "table1_baseline_characteristics.csv", "kind": "csv", "exists": true, "bytes": 6101, "rows": 65, "columns": [{"name": "variable", "type": ""}, {"name": "level", "type": ""}, {"name": "full_pravastatin", "type": ""}, {"name": "full_no_pravastatin", "type": ""}, {"name": "smd_full", "type": ""}, {"name": "matched_pravastatin", "type": ""}, {"name": "matched_no_pravastatin", "type": ""}, {"name": "smd_matched", "type": ""}, {"name": "smd_iptw", "type": ""}]}]}, {"step": 18, "file": "a18_km_matched.py", "code": "\"\"\"\nAnalysis step 18. Kaplan-Meier survival in the matched cohort\n\nInput     : matched_cohorts.parquet, analysis_cohort.parquet\nOperation : Per imputation's matched cohort: Kaplan-Meier survival (primary outcome\n            time28_all/death28_all) by group on days 0-28 and log-rank test; survival averaged\n            across imputations, median log-rank p. Unmatched (full cohort) KM for reference.\nOutput    : km_survival_estimates.csv\n\"\"\"\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nfrom lifelines import KaplanMeierFitter\nfrom lifelines.statistics import logrank_test\n\nfrom common import DURATION, EVENT, EXPOSURE, log, read_parquet, write_csv\n\nDAYS = np.arange(0, 29)\nGROUPS = {1: \"pravastatin\", 0: \"no_pravastatin\"}\n\n\ndef km_at(d):\n    return KaplanMeierFitter().fit(d[DURATION], d[EVENT]).survival_function_at_times(DAYS).to_numpy()\n\n\ndef main():\n    m = read_parquet(\"matched_cohorts.parquet\")\n    full = read_parquet(\"analysis_cohort.parquet\")\n    pvals, surv = [], {g: [] for g in GROUPS}\n    for _, d in m.groupby(\"imputation\"):\n        for g in GROUPS:\n            surv[g].append(km_at(d[d[EXPOSURE] == g]))\n        e, u = d[d[EXPOSURE] == 1], d[d[EXPOSURE] == 0]\n        pvals.append(logrank_test(e[DURATION], u[DURATION], e[EVENT], u[EVENT]).p_value)\n    rows = []\n    for g, lab in GROUPS.items():\n        s = np.array(surv[g])\n        sf = km_at(full[full[EXPOSURE] == g])\n        for i, t in enumerate(DAYS):\n            rows.append({\"group\": lab, \"day\": int(t), \"survival_matched\": s[:, i].mean(),\n                         \"survival_matched_min_over_imp\": s[:, i].min(),\n                         \"survival_matched_max_over_imp\": s[:, i].max(), \"survival_unmatched\": sf[i]})\n    out = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n    out[\"matched_logrank_p_median\"] = float(np.median(pvals))\n    write_csv(out, \"km_survival_estimates.csv\")\n    d28 = out[out.day == 28].set_index(\"group\")\n    log(\"a18\", \"28-day all-cause mortality (matched): \" + \", \".join(\n        f\"{g} {1 - r.survival_matched:.1%}\" for g, r in d28.iterrows()) + f\"; log-rank p (median)={np.median(pvals):.3g}\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n", "outputs": [{"name": "km_survival_estimates.csv", "kind": "csv", "exists": true, "bytes": 6578, "rows": 58, "columns": [{"name": "group", "type": ""}, {"name": "day", "type": ""}, {"name": "survival_matched", "type": ""}, {"name": "survival_matched_min_over_imp", "type": ""}, {"name": "survival_matched_max_over_imp", "type": ""}, {"name": "survival_unmatched", "type": ""}, {"name": "matched_logrank_p_median", "type": ""}]}]}, {"step": 19, "file": "a19_primary_cox_matched.py", "code": "\"\"\"\nAnalysis step 19. Primary Cox regression in the matched cohort\n\nInput     : matched_cohorts.parquet, matched_balance.csv\nOperation : Per imputation's matched cohort, Cox (time28_all, death28_all) on pravastatin_exposed\n            with robust variance clustered on pair_id (Efron ties); Rubin pooling -> primary HR.\n            Supplementary: same model additionally adjusted for covariates whose averaged matched\n            SMD >= 0.10 (residual imbalance), as matched-cohort adjusted models in published studies.\nOutput    : primary_cox_results.csv\n\"\"\"\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\nfrom common import DURATION, EVENT, EXPOSURE, cox_exposure, hr_row, log, read_csv, read_json, \\\n    read_parquet, rubin, write_csv\n\n\ndef counts(d):\n    return {\"n_exposed\": int(d[EXPOSURE].sum()), \"deaths_exposed\": int(d.loc[d[EXPOSURE] == 1, EVENT].sum()),\n            \"n_unexposed\": int((1 - d[EXPOSURE]).sum()),\n            \"deaths_unexposed\": int(d.loc[d[EXPOSURE] == 0, EVENT].sum())}\n\n\ndef main():\n    sp = read_json(\"analysis_variable_specification.json\")\n    m = read_parquet(\"matched_cohorts.parquet\")\n    bal = read_csv(\"matched_balance.csv\")\n    resid = [c for c in bal.loc[~bal.balanced, \"covariate\"]]\n    cont = sp[\"ps_covariates\"][\"continuous\"]\n    adj_cols = []\n    for c in resid:\n        if \"=\" in c:\n            var, lev = c.split(\"=\", 1)\n            col = f\"adj_{len(adj_cols)}\"\n            m[col] = (m[var] == lev).astype(float)\n        else:\n            col = sp[\"transformed_names\"].get(c, c) if c in cont else c\n        adj_cols.append(col)\n\n    b0, v0, b1, v1 = [], [], [], []\n    for _, d in m.groupby(\"imputation\"):\n        b, v, _ = cox_exposure(d, DURATION, EVENT, None, cluster=\"pair_id\")\n        b0.append(b); v0.append(v)\n        if adj_cols:\n            b, v, _ = cox_exposure(d, DURATION, EVENT, None, covariates=adj_cols, cluster=\"pair_id\")\n            b1.append(b); v1.append(v)\n    n = int(m.imputation.value_counts().iloc[0])\n    d1 = m[m.imputation == 1]\n    rows = [hr_row(\"Primary: 1:1 PSM, Cox (pair-clustered)\", rubin(b0, v0, n), population=\"PS-matched cohort\",\n                   outcome=\"28-day all-cause mortality\", comparison=\"pravastatin vs no pravastatin\",\n                   note=\"primary analysis\", **counts(d1))]\n    if adj_cols:\n        rows.append(hr_row(\"PSM + adjustment for residual imbalance\", rubin(b1, v1, n),\n                           population=\"PS-matched cohort\", outcome=\"28-day all-cause mortality\",\n                           comparison=\"pravastatin vs no pravastatin\",\n                           note=\"adjusted for \" + \", \".join(resid), **counts(d1)))\n    out = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n    write_csv(out, \"primary_cox_results.csv\")\n    for r in out.itertuples():\n        log(\"a19\", f\"{r.analysis}: HR {r.estimate:.3f} ({r.ci_low:.3f}-{r.ci_high:.3f}), p={r.p_value:.3g}; \"\n                   f\"deaths {r.deaths_exposed}/{r.n_exposed} vs {r.deaths_unexposed}/{r.n_unexposed}\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n", "outputs": [{"name": "primary_cox_results.csv", "kind": "csv", "exists": true, "bytes": 641, "rows": 2, "columns": [{"name": "analysis", "type": ""}, {"name": "effect_measure", "type": ""}, {"name": "estimate", "type": ""}, {"name": "ci_low", "type": ""}, {"name": "ci_high", "type": ""}, {"name": "p_value", "type": ""}, {"name": "status", "type": ""}, {"name": "population", "type": ""}, {"name": "outcome", "type": ""}, {"name": "comparison", "type": ""}, {"name": "note", "type": ""}, {"name": "n_exposed", "type": ""}, {"name": "deaths_exposed", "type": ""}, {"name": "n_unexposed", "type": ""}, {"name": "deaths_unexposed", "type": ""}]}]}, {"step": 20, "file": "a20_ph_test.py", "code": "\"\"\"\nAnalysis step 20. Proportional-hazards assessment\n\nInput     : matched_cohorts.parquet\nOperation : Refit the primary matched Cox model per imputation and test PH for pravastatin_exposed\n            (lifelines proportional_hazard_test, rank and log time). time28_all of 0 set to 0.001\n            day (order-preserving) so log(time) exists. If median p (rank) < 0.05, the matched\n            28-day risk difference and odds ratio become the primary effect measures (a22 reports them).\nOutput    : proportional_hazards_test.csv\n\"\"\"\nimport pandas as pd\nfrom lifelines.statistics import proportional_hazard_test\n\nfrom common import DURATION, EVENT, EXPOSURE, cox_exposure, log, read_parquet, write_csv\n\n\ndef main():\n    m = read_parquet(\"matched_cohorts.parquet\")\n    m[DURATION] = m[DURATION].clip(lower=1e-3)\n    rows = []\n    for k, d in m.groupby(\"imputation\"):\n        _, _, cph = cox_exposure(d, DURATION, EVENT, None, cluster=\"pair_id\")\n        data = d[[DURATION, EVENT, EXPOSURE, \"pair_id\"]]\n        for tt in (\"rank\", \"log\"):\n            s = proportional_hazard_test(cph, data, time_transform=tt).summary\n            rows.append({\"imputation\": k, \"time_transform\": tt,\n                         \"test_statistic\": float(s.loc[EXPOSURE, \"test_statistic\"]),\n                         \"p_value\": float(s.loc[EXPOSURE, \"p\"])})\n    out = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n    med = out[out.time_transform == \"rank\"].p_value.median()\n    out[\"median_p_rank\"] = med\n    out[\"median_p_log\"] = out[out.time_transform == \"log\"].p_value.median()\n    out[\"ph_violated\"] = bool(med < 0.05)\n    write_csv(out, \"proportional_hazards_test.csv\")\n    log(\"a20\", f\"median p (rank)={med:.3g}, (log)={out.median_p_log.iloc[0]:.3g}; ph_violated={med < 0.05}\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n", "outputs": [{"name": "proportional_hazards_test.csv", "kind": "csv", "exists": true, "bytes": 3715, "rows": 40, "columns": [{"name": "imputation", "type": ""}, {"name": "time_transform", "type": ""}, {"name": "test_statistic", "type": ""}, {"name": "p_value", "type": ""}, {"name": "median_p_rank", "type": ""}, {"name": "median_p_log", "type": ""}, {"name": "ph_violated", "type": ""}]}]}, {"step": 21, "file": "a21_multivariable_cox.py", "code": "\"\"\"\nAnalysis step 21. Multivariable Cox models in the full cohort\n\nInput     : imputed_cohorts.parquet\nOperation : Per imputation, Cox models of the primary outcome in the full cohort (robust variance),\n            pooled by Rubin: Model 1 unadjusted; Model 2 age, sex, race_group; Model 3 all PS\n            covariates (z-scored continuous, binaries, one-hot categories).\nOutput    : multivariable_cox_results.csv\n\"\"\"\nimport pandas as pd\n\nfrom common import DURATION, EVENT, EXPOSURE, cox_exposure, design_matrix, hr_row, log, read_json, \\\n    read_parquet, rubin, write_csv\n\n\ndef model_frame(d, sp, which):\n    if which == 1:\n        return d[[DURATION, EVENT, EXPOSURE]].copy(), []\n    if which == 2:\n        sub = {\"ps_covariates\": {\"continuous\": [\"age\"], \"binary\": [\"female\"],\n                                 \"categorical\": {\"race_group\": \"White\"}}, \"transformed_names\": {}}\n        X, names = design_matrix(d, sub)\n    else:\n        X, names = design_matrix(d, sp)\n    cols = [f\"x{i}\" for i in range(len(names))]\n    f = pd.DataFrame(X, columns=cols, index=d.index)\n    f[[DURATION, EVENT, EXPOSURE]] = d[[DURATION, EVENT, EXPOSURE]]\n    return f, cols\n\n\ndef main():\n    sp = read_json(\"analysis_variable_specification.json\")\n    imp = read_parquet(\"imputed_cohorts.parquet\")\n    labels = {1: \"Model 1: unadjusted Cox\", 2: \"Model 2: Cox adjusted for age, sex, race\",\n              3: \"Model 3: Cox adjusted for all PS covariates\"}\n    d1 = imp[imp.imputation == 1]\n    cnt = {\"n_exposed\": int(d1[EXPOSURE].sum()), \"deaths_exposed\": int(d1.loc[d1[EXPOSURE] == 1, EVENT].sum()),\n           \"n_unexposed\": int((1 - d1[EXPOSURE]).sum()),\n           \"deaths_unexposed\": int(d1.loc[d1[EXPOSURE] == 0, EVENT].sum())}\n    rows = []\n    for which, lab in labels.items():\n        b_list, v_list = [], []\n        for _, d in imp.groupby(\"imputation\"):\n            f, cols = model_frame(d, sp, which)\n            b, v, _ = cox_exposure(f, DURATION, EVENT, None, covariates=cols)\n            b_list.append(b); v_list.append(v)\n            if which == 1:          # no imputed variables involved; one fit suffices\n                b_list, v_list = b_list * 2, v_list * 2\n                break\n        rows.append(hr_row(lab, rubin(b_list, v_list, len(d1)), population=\"full cohort\",\n                           outcome=\"28-day all-cause mortality\", comparison=\"pravastatin vs no pravastatin\",\n                           **cnt))\n    out = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n    write_csv(out, \"multivariable_cox_results.csv\")\n    for r in out.itertuples():\n        log(\"a21\", f\"{r.analysis}: HR {r.estimate:.3f} ({r.ci_low:.3f}-{r.ci_high:.3f})\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n", "outputs": [{"name": "multivariable_cox_results.csv", "kind": "csv", "exists": true, "bytes": 795, "rows": 3, "columns": [{"name": "analysis", "type": ""}, {"name": "effect_measure", "type": ""}, {"name": "estimate", "type": ""}, {"name": "ci_low", "type": ""}, {"name": "ci_high", "type": ""}, {"name": "p_value", "type": ""}, {"name": "status", "type": ""}, {"name": "population", "type": ""}, {"name": "outcome", "type": ""}, {"name": "comparison", "type": ""}, {"name": "n_exposed", "type": ""}, {"name": "deaths_exposed", "type": ""}, {"name": "n_unexposed", "type": ""}, {"name": "deaths_unexposed", "type": ""}]}]}, {"step": 22, "file": "a22_secondary_outcomes.py", "code": "\"\"\"\nAnalysis step 22. Secondary outcomes in the matched cohort\n\nInput     : matched_cohorts.parquet, proportional_hazards_test.csv\nOperation : Per imputation's matched cohort, pooled by Rubin:\n            - 90-day all-cause mortality: Cox (pair-clustered robust variance)\n            - 28-day all-cause mortality: odds ratio and risk difference (pair-clustered sandwich);\n              marked primary effect measure if the PH test failed\n            - in-hospital and ICU mortality: logistic regression, pair-clustered sandwich (OR)\n            ICU and hospital LOS: median (IQR) by group and Mann-Whitney test (imputation 1 matched set).\nOutput    : secondary_outcome_results.csv\n\"\"\"\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nfrom scipy import stats\n\nfrom common import EXPOSURE, cox_exposure, hr_row, log, read_csv, read_parquet, rubin, weighted_logit_hc0, \\\n    write_csv\n\n\ndef counts(d, ev):\n    return {\"n_exposed\": int(d[EXPOSURE].sum()), \"deaths_exposed\": int(d.loc[d[EXPOSURE] == 1, ev].sum()),\n            \"n_unexposed\": int((1 - d[EXPOSURE]).sum()), \"deaths_unexposed\": int(d.loc[d[EXPOSURE] == 0, ev].sum())}\n\n\ndef clustered_rd(y, a, cluster):\n    p1, p0 = y[a == 1].mean(), y[a == 0].mean()\n    # influence-function sandwich for the difference in means, summed within pairs\n    n1, n0 = (a == 1).sum(), (a == 0).sum()\n    infl = np.where(a == 1, (y - p1) / n1, -(y - p0) / n0)\n    s = pd.Series(infl).groupby(np.asarray(cluster)).sum().to_numpy()\n    return p1 - p0, float(np.sum(s ** 2))\n\n\ndef main():\n    m = read_parquet(\"matched_cohorts.parquet\")\n    ph_fail = bool(read_csv(\"proportional_hazards_test.csv\").ph_violated.iloc[0])\n    n = int(m.imputation.value_counts().iloc[0])\n    d1 = m[m.imputation == 1]\n    rows = []\n\n    b, v = [], []\n    for _, d in m.groupby(\"imputation\"):\n        bb, vv, _ = cox_exposure(d, \"time90_all\", \"death90_all\", None, cluster=\"pair_id\")\n        b.append(bb); v.append(vv)\n    rows.append(hr_row(\"90-day all-cause mortality, PSM Cox\", rubin(b, v, n), population=\"PS-matched cohort\",\n                       outcome=\"90-day all-cause mortality\", comparison=\"pravastatin vs no pravastatin\",\n                       **counts(d1, \"death90_all\")))\n\n    for ev, outcome in ((\"death28_all\", \"28-day all-cause mortality (binary)\"),\n                        (\"hosp_death\", \"in-hospital mortality\"), (\"icu_death\", \"ICU mortality\")):\n        lo_b, lo_v, rd_b, rd_v = [], [], [], []\n        for _, d in m.groupby(\"imputation\"):\n            y = d[ev].to_numpy().astype(float)\n            a = d[EXPOSURE].to_numpy().astype(float)\n            bb, vv = weighted_logit_hc0(y, a, np.ones(len(y)), cluster=d.pair_id.to_numpy())\n            lo_b.append(bb); lo_v.append(vv)\n            r, rv = clustered_rd(y, a, d.pair_id.to_numpy())\n            rd_b.append(r); rd_v.append(rv)\n        role = \"primary effect measure (PH violated)\" if (ev == \"death28_all\" and ph_fail) else \"\"\n        for key, est, var, tf in ((\"OR\", lo_b, lo_v, np.exp), (\"RD\", rd_b, rd_v, lambda x: x)):\n            r = rubin(est, var, n)\n            rows.append({\"analysis\": f\"{outcome}, PSM {key}\", \"population\": \"PS-matched cohort\", \"outcome\": outcome,\n                         \"comparison\": \"pravastatin vs no pravastatin\", \"effect_measure\": key,\n                         \"estimate\": tf(r[\"est\"]), \"ci_low\": tf(r[\"lo\"]), \"ci_high\": tf(r[\"hi\"]),\n                         \"p_value\": r[\"p\"], \"status\": \"estimated\", \"note\": role, **counts(d1, ev)})\n\n    for col, outcome in ((\"icu_los_days\", \"ICU length of stay (days)\"), (\"hosp_los_days\", \"hospital length of stay (days)\")):\n        e, u = d1.loc[d1[EXPOSURE] == 1, col].dropna(), d1.loc[d1[EXPOSURE] == 0, col].dropna()\n        p = stats.mannwhitneyu(e, u, alternative=\"two-sided\").pvalue\n        rows.append({\"analysis\": f\"{outcome}, PSM (imputation 1 matched set)\", \"population\": \"PS-matched cohort\",\n                     \"outcome\": outcome, \"comparison\": \"pravastatin vs no pravastatin\",\n                     \"effect_measure\": \"median difference\", \"estimate\": e.median() - u.median(),\n                     \"ci_low\": np.nan, \"ci_high\": np.nan, \"p_value\": p, \"status\": \"estimated\",\n                     \"note\": f\"median (IQR) {e.median():.1f} ({e.quantile(.25):.1f}-{e.quantile(.75):.1f}) vs \"\n                             f\"{u.median():.1f} ({u.quantile(.25):.1f}-{u.quantile(.75):.1f}); Mann-Whitney\",\n                     \"n_exposed\": len(e), \"n_unexposed\": len(u)})\n    out = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n    write_csv(out, \"secondary_outcome_results.csv\")\n    for r in out.itertuples():\n        log(\"a22\", f\"{r.analysis}: {r.effect_measure} {r.estimate:.3f}\"\n                   + (f\" ({r.ci_low:.3f}-{r.ci_high:.3f})\" if pd.notna(r.ci_low) else \"\") + f\", p={r.p_value:.3g}\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n", "outputs": [{"name": "secondary_outcome_results.csv", "kind": "csv", "exists": true, "bytes": 2241, "rows": 9, "columns": [{"name": "analysis", "type": ""}, {"name": "effect_measure", "type": ""}, {"name": "estimate", "type": ""}, {"name": "ci_low", "type": ""}, {"name": "ci_high", "type": ""}, {"name": "p_value", "type": ""}, {"name": "status", "type": ""}, {"name": "population", "type": ""}, {"name": "outcome", "type": ""}, {"name": "comparison", "type": ""}, {"name": "n_exposed", "type": ""}, {"name": "deaths_exposed", "type": ""}, {"name": "n_unexposed", "type": ""}, {"name": "deaths_unexposed", "type": ""}, {"name": "note", "type": ""}]}]}, {"step": 23, "file": "a23_subgroups.py", "code": "\"\"\"\nAnalysis step 23. Subgroup analyses (matched cohort)\n\nInput     : matched_cohorts.parquet\nOperation : For age_group (<65, >=65), sex, sofa_tertile (SAPS II substitute), charlson_group,\n            septic_shock and organ_failure_any: per imputation's matched cohort, Cox with exposure,\n            subgroup indicators and exposure x subgroup interactions (pair-clustered robust variance).\n            Stratum log HR = b_exposure (+ b_interaction); pooled by Rubin; interaction by pooled\n            multivariate Wald (D1). Strata with < 5 deaths in either group -> not_estimable.\nOutput    : subgroup_results.csv\n\"\"\"\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nfrom lifelines import CoxPHFitter\n\nfrom common import DURATION, EVENT, EXPOSURE, log, read_parquet, rubin, rubin_wald, write_csv\n\nSUBGROUPS = [\"age_group\", \"sex\", \"sofa_tertile\", \"charlson_group\", \"septic_shock\", \"organ_failure_any\"]\nMIN_DEATHS = 5\n\n\ndef main():\n    m = read_parquet(\"matched_cohorts.parquet\")\n    n_obs = int(m.imputation.value_counts().iloc[0])\n    rows = []\n    for sg in SUBGROUPS:\n        levels = sorted(m[sg].unique())\n        ref, others = levels[0], levels[1:]\n        se = {lev: [] for lev in levels}\n        sv = {lev: [] for lev in levels}\n        ie, ic = [], []\n        cnt = {lev: {\"n_exposed\": [], \"deaths_exposed\": [], \"n_unexposed\": [], \"deaths_unexposed\": []}\n               for lev in levels}\n        for _, d in m.groupby(\"imputation\"):\n            X = d[[DURATION, EVENT, EXPOSURE, \"pair_id\"]].copy()\n            inter = []\n            for i, lev in enumerate(others):\n                X[f\"sg{i}\"] = (d[sg] == lev).astype(float).to_numpy()\n                X[f\"int{i}\"] = X[f\"sg{i}\"] * X[EXPOSURE]\n                inter.append(f\"int{i}\")\n            cph = CoxPHFitter().fit(X, DURATION, EVENT, robust=True, cluster_col=\"pair_id\")\n            V, b = cph.variance_matrix_, cph.params_\n            se[ref].append(b[EXPOSURE]); sv[ref].append(V.loc[EXPOSURE, EXPOSURE])\n            for i, lev in enumerate(others):\n                t = f\"int{i}\"\n                se[lev].append(b[EXPOSURE] + b[t])\n                sv[lev].append(V.loc[EXPOSURE, EXPOSURE] + V.loc[t, t] + 2 * V.loc[EXPOSURE, t])\n            ie.append(b[inter].to_numpy()); ic.append(V.loc[inter, inter].to_numpy())\n            for lev in levels:\n                s = d[d[sg] == lev]\n                cnt[lev][\"n_exposed\"].append(int(s[EXPOSURE].sum()))\n                cnt[lev][\"deaths_exposed\"].append(int(s.loc[s[EXPOSURE] == 1, EVENT].sum()))\n                cnt[lev][\"n_unexposed\"].append(int((1 - s[EXPOSURE]).sum()))\n                cnt[lev][\"deaths_unexposed\"].append(int(s.loc[s[EXPOSURE] == 0, EVENT].sum()))\n        wald = rubin_wald(ie, ic)\n        for lev in levels:\n            c = {k: int(round(np.mean(v))) for k, v in cnt[lev].items()}     # mean over imputations\n            ok = min(c[\"deaths_exposed\"], c[\"deaths_unexposed\"]) >= MIN_DEATHS\n            r = rubin(se[lev], sv[lev], n_obs)\n            rows.append({\"subgroup\": sg, \"level\": lev, **c, \"effect_measure\": \"HR\",\n                         \"estimate\": np.exp(r[\"est\"]) if ok else np.nan,\n                         \"ci_low\": np.exp(r[\"lo\"]) if ok else np.nan,\n                         \"ci_high\": np.exp(r[\"hi\"]) if ok else np.nan,\n                         \"p_value\": r[\"p\"] if ok else np.nan, \"p_interaction\": wald[\"p\"],\n                         \"status\": \"estimated\" if ok else f\"not_estimable (<{MIN_DEATHS} deaths in a group)\"})\n    out = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n    write_csv(out, \"subgroup_results.csv\")\n    for r in out.itertuples():\n        est = f\"HR {r.estimate:.2f} ({r.ci_low:.2f}-{r.ci_high:.2f})\" if r.status == \"estimated\" else r.status\n        log(\"a23\", f\"{r.subgroup}={r.level}: deaths {r.deaths_exposed}/{r.n_exposed} vs \"\n                   f\"{r.deaths_unexposed}/{r.n_unexposed}; {est}; p_int={r.p_interaction:.3g}\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n", "outputs": [{"name": "subgroup_results.csv", "kind": "csv", "exists": true, "bytes": 1980, "rows": 13, "columns": [{"name": "subgroup", "type": ""}, {"name": "level", "type": ""}, {"name": "n_exposed", "type": ""}, {"name": "deaths_exposed", "type": ""}, {"name": "n_unexposed", "type": ""}, {"name": "deaths_unexposed", "type": ""}, {"name": "effect_measure", "type": ""}, {"name": "estimate", "type": ""}, {"name": "ci_low", "type": ""}, {"name": "ci_high", "type": ""}, {"name": "p_value", "type": ""}, {"name": "p_interaction", "type": ""}, {"name": "status", "type": ""}]}]}, {"step": 24, "file": "a24_sensitivity_confounding.py", "code": "\"\"\"\nAnalysis step 24. Sensitivity analyses: alternative confounding control\n\nInput     : iptw_cohort.parquet, analysis_cohort.parquet, analysis_variable_specification.json\nOperation : Pooled Cox HRs for the primary outcome (time28_all, death28_all):\n            (a) stabilized truncated IPTW (design-specified ATE)   (b) untruncated stabilized IPTW\n            (c) overlap weights                                   (d) 1:1 PSM, caliper 0.2 SD of logit PS\n            (e) complete-case 1:1 PSM (no imputation)             (f) PSM within prior_statin_use == 0\n            (g) PSM within prior_statin_use == 1  [(f), (g): PS re-estimated in the subset]\n            Weighted models use robust variance; matched models pair-clustered robust variance.\nOutput    : sensitivity_confounding_results.csv\n\"\"\"\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\nfrom common import CALIPER_PS, DURATION, EVENT, EXPOSURE, cox_exposure, hr_row, log, matched_frame, \\\n    max_smd_unweighted, max_weighted_smd, model_continuous, ps_and_weights, read_json, read_parquet, rubin, write_csv\n\n\ndef counts(d):\n    return {\"n_exposed\": int(d[EXPOSURE].sum()), \"deaths_exposed\": int(d.loc[d[EXPOSURE] == 1, EVENT].sum()),\n            \"n_unexposed\": int((1 - d[EXPOSURE]).sum()),\n            \"deaths_unexposed\": int(d.loc[d[EXPOSURE] == 0, EVENT].sum())}\n\n\ndef main():\n    sp = read_json(\"analysis_variable_specification.json\")\n    df = read_parquet(\"iptw_cohort.parquet\")\n    full1 = df[df.imputation == 1]\n    rows = []\n\n    def add(label, b, v, n, smds, pop, cnt):\n        rows.append(hr_row(label, rubin(b, v, n), population=pop, outcome=\"28-day all-cause mortality\",\n                           comparison=\"pravastatin vs no pravastatin\", max_smd=float(np.mean(smds)),\n                           note=f\"max SMD {np.mean(smds):.3f}\", **cnt))\n\n    for col, label in ((\"sw\", \"(a) stabilized IPTW, truncated (design-specified ATE)\"),\n                       (\"sw_raw\", \"(b) stabilized IPTW, untruncated\"), (\"ow\", \"(c) overlap weights\")):\n        b, v, s = [], [], []\n        for _, d in df.groupby(\"imputation\"):\n            bb, vv, _ = cox_exposure(d, DURATION, EVENT, col)\n            b.append(bb); v.append(vv); s.append(max_weighted_smd(d, sp, d[col].to_numpy()))\n        add(label, b, v, len(full1), s, \"full cohort (weighted)\", counts(full1))\n\n    b, v, s, mlast = [], [], [], None\n    for _, d in df.groupby(\"imputation\"):\n        d = d.reset_index(drop=True)\n        logit = np.log(d.ps / (1 - d.ps))\n        m = matched_frame(d.drop(columns=\"ps\"), d.ps.to_numpy(), 0.2 * logit.std(), \"logit\")\n        bb, vv, _ = cox_exposure(m, DURATION, EVENT, None, cluster=\"pair_id\")\n        b.append(bb); v.append(vv); s.append(max_smd_unweighted(m, sp)); mlast = m\n    add(\"(d) 1:1 PSM, caliper 0.2 SD of logit PS\", b, v, len(mlast), s, \"PS-matched cohort\", counts(mlast))\n\n    cohort = read_parquet(\"analysis_cohort.parquet\")\n    cc = cohort.dropna(subset=model_continuous(sp)).reset_index(drop=True)\n    pw = ps_and_weights(cc, sp)\n    m = matched_frame(cc, pw[\"ps\"], CALIPER_PS, \"ps\")\n    bb, vv, _ = cox_exposure(m, DURATION, EVENT, None, cluster=\"pair_id\")\n    add(f\"(e) complete-case 1:1 PSM (n={len(cc)})\", [bb], [vv], len(m), [max_smd_unweighted(m, sp)],\n        \"complete cases, PS-matched\", counts(m))\n\n    for val, lab in ((0, \"(f) no prior statin use\"), (1, \"(g) prior statin use\")):\n        b, v, s, mlast = [], [], [], None\n        for _, d in df[df.prior_statin_use == val].groupby(\"imputation\"):\n            d = d.drop(columns=[\"ps\"]).reset_index(drop=True)\n            pw = ps_and_weights(d, sp, drop=(\"prior_statin_use\",))\n            m = matched_frame(d, pw[\"ps\"], CALIPER_PS, \"ps\")\n            bb, vv, _ = cox_exposure(m, DURATION, EVENT, None, cluster=\"pair_id\")\n            b.append(bb); v.append(vv); s.append(max_smd_unweighted(m, sp)); mlast = m\n        add(f\"{lab}, PSM with PS re-estimated\", b, v, len(mlast), s, f\"prior_statin_use={val}, PS-matched\",\n            counts(mlast))\n\n    out = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n    write_csv(out, \"sensitivity_confounding_results.csv\")\n    for r in out.itertuples():\n        log(\"a24\", f\"{r.analysis}: HR {r.estimate:.3f} ({r.ci_low:.3f}-{r.ci_high:.3f}) max SMD {r.max_smd:.3f}\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n", "outputs": [{"name": "sensitivity_confounding_results.csv", "kind": "csv", "exists": true, "bytes": 2008, "rows": 7, "columns": [{"name": "analysis", "type": ""}, {"name": "effect_measure", "type": ""}, {"name": "estimate", "type": ""}, {"name": "ci_low", "type": ""}, {"name": "ci_high", "type": ""}, {"name": "p_value", "type": ""}, {"name": "status", "type": ""}, {"name": "population", "type": ""}, {"name": "outcome", "type": ""}, {"name": "comparison", "type": ""}, {"name": "max_smd", "type": ""}, {"name": "note", "type": ""}, {"name": "n_exposed", "type": ""}, {"name": "deaths_exposed", "type": ""}, {"name": "n_unexposed", "type": ""}, {"name": "deaths_unexposed", "type": ""}]}]}, {"step": 25, "file": "a25_sensitivity_immortal_time.py", "code": "\"\"\"\nAnalysis step 25. Sensitivity analyses: immortal time\n\nInput     : analysis_cohort.parquet, imputed_cohorts.parquet, analysis_variable_specification.json\nOperation : (h) 48-hour landmark: patients alive at 48 h (time28_all > 2); follow-up restarts at\n            the landmark (lm_days = time28_all - 2); re-impute (MICE m=20), re-estimate PS,\n            1:1 PSM (caliper 0.05) and pair-clustered Cox; pooled.\n            (i) Time-dependent exposure: full cohort, follow-up split at hours_to_first_pravastatin\n            so exposure switches 0 -> 1 at initiation; lifelines CoxTimeVaryingFitter adjusted for\n            all PS covariates (z-scored) per imputation; pooled.\nOutput    : sensitivity_immortal_time_results.csv\n\"\"\"\nimport time\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nfrom lifelines import CoxTimeVaryingFitter\n\nfrom common import CALIPER_PS, DURATION, EVENT, EXPOSURE, cox_exposure, design_matrix, hr_row, log, \\\n    matched_frame, max_smd_unweighted, mice, ps_and_weights, read_json, read_parquet, rubin, write_csv\n\nLANDMARK_DAYS = 2.0\n\n\ndef counts(d, ev=EVENT):\n    return {\"n_exposed\": int(d[EXPOSURE].sum()), \"deaths_exposed\": int(d.loc[d[EXPOSURE] == 1, ev].sum()),\n            \"n_unexposed\": int((1 - d[EXPOSURE]).sum()), \"deaths_unexposed\": int(d.loc[d[EXPOSURE] == 0, ev].sum())}\n\n\ndef landmark(sp):\n    df = read_parquet(\"analysis_cohort.parquet\")\n    lm = df[df[DURATION] > LANDMARK_DAYS].copy()\n    lm[\"lm_days\"] = lm[DURATION] - LANDMARK_DAYS\n    imp = mice(lm, sp, duration=\"lm_days\")\n    b, v, s, mlast = [], [], [], None\n    for _, d in imp.groupby(\"imputation\"):\n        d = d.reset_index(drop=True)\n        pw = ps_and_weights(d, sp)\n        m = matched_frame(d, pw[\"ps\"], CALIPER_PS, \"ps\")\n        bb, vv, _ = cox_exposure(m, \"lm_days\", EVENT, None, cluster=\"pair_id\")\n        b.append(bb); v.append(vv); s.append(max_smd_unweighted(m, sp)); mlast = m\n    return hr_row(\"(h) 48-hour landmark, 1:1 PSM Cox\", rubin(b, v, len(mlast)),\n                  population=f\"alive at 48 h (n={len(lm)}), PS-matched\", outcome=\"death from 48 h to day 28\",\n                  comparison=\"pravastatin vs no pravastatin\", note=f\"max SMD {np.mean(s):.3f}\", **counts(mlast))\n\n\ndef time_dependent(sp):\n    imp = read_parquet(\"imputed_cohorts.parquet\")\n    b, v, n_edge = [], [], 0\n    for k, d in imp.groupby(\"imputation\"):\n        d = d.reset_index(drop=True)\n        X, names = design_matrix(d, sp)\n        cols = [f\"x{i}\" for i in range(len(names))]\n        cov = pd.DataFrame(X, columns=cols)\n        t_exp = (d.hours_to_first_pravastatin / 24).to_numpy()\n        T = np.maximum(d[DURATION].to_numpy(), 1e-3)\n        E = d[EVENT].to_numpy()\n        split = (d[EXPOSURE].to_numpy() == 1) & (t_exp < T)\n        if k == 1:\n            n_edge = int(((d[EXPOSURE] == 1) & ~split).sum())\n        base = pd.concat([pd.DataFrame({\"id\": np.arange(len(d))}), cov], axis=1)\n        unexp = base.assign(start=0.0, stop=np.where(split, np.maximum(t_exp, 1e-4), T),\n                            event=np.where(split, 0, E), exposure=np.where(split, 0, d[EXPOSURE].to_numpy()))\n        exp_part = base[split].assign(start=np.maximum(t_exp[split], 1e-4), stop=T[split], event=E[split], exposure=1)\n        long = pd.concat([unexp, exp_part], ignore_index=True)\n        long = long[long.stop > long.start]\n        ctv = CoxTimeVaryingFitter(penalizer=0.0)\n        ctv.fit(long, id_col=\"id\", event_col=\"event\", start_col=\"start\", stop_col=\"stop\")\n        b.append(float(ctv.params_[\"exposure\"]))\n        v.append(float(ctv.summary.loc[\"exposure\", \"se(coef)\"]) ** 2)\n    d1 = imp[imp.imputation == 1]\n    return hr_row(\"(i) time-dependent exposure Cox, adjusted for PS covariates\", rubin(b, v, len(d1)),\n                  population=\"full cohort\", outcome=\"28-day all-cause mortality\",\n                  comparison=\"pravastatin (from initiation) vs not yet / never\",\n                  note=f\"exposed with initiation at/after end of follow-up kept unexposed: {n_edge}\",\n                  **counts(d1))\n\n\ndef main():\n    t0 = time.time()\n    sp = read_json(\"analysis_variable_specification.json\")\n    rows = [landmark(sp), time_dependent(sp)]\n    out = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n    write_csv(out, \"sensitivity_immortal_time_results.csv\")\n    for r in out.itertuples():\n        log(\"a25\", f\"{r.analysis}: HR {r.estimate:.3f} ({r.ci_low:.3f}-{r.ci_high:.3f}); {r.note}\")\n    log(\"a25\", f\"({time.time() - t0:.0f}s)\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n", "outputs": [{"name": "sensitivity_immortal_time_results.csv", "kind": "csv", "exists": true, "bytes": 727, "rows": 2, "columns": [{"name": "analysis", "type": ""}, {"name": "effect_measure", "type": ""}, {"name": "estimate", "type": ""}, {"name": "ci_low", "type": ""}, {"name": "ci_high", "type": ""}, {"name": "p_value", "type": ""}, {"name": "status", "type": ""}, {"name": "population", "type": ""}, {"name": "outcome", "type": ""}, {"name": "comparison", "type": ""}, {"name": "note", "type": ""}, {"name": "n_exposed", "type": ""}, {"name": "deaths_exposed", "type": ""}, {"name": "n_unexposed", "type": ""}, {"name": "deaths_unexposed", "type": ""}]}]}, {"step": 26, "file": "a26_design_outcome.py", "code": "\"\"\"\nAnalysis step 26. Design-specified in-hospital outcome and competing risks\n\nInput     : matched_cohorts.parquet\nOperation : Design outcome (followup_days, death_28d; discharged alive censored at discharge):\n            pair-clustered Cox in each matched cohort. Fine-Gray: event_status 1 = death,\n            2 = discharge alive (competing); only administrative censoring at day 28 exists, so\n            competing-event patients stay in the risk set to day 28 (duration 28, event 0).\n            Matched-cohort cumulative incidence of death at day 28 (Aalen-Johansen). Rubin pooling.\nOutput    : design_outcome_results.csv\n\"\"\"\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nfrom lifelines import AalenJohansenFitter\n\nfrom common import DESIGN_DURATION, DESIGN_EVENT, EXPOSURE, cox_exposure, hr_row, log, read_parquet, rubin, \\\n    write_csv\n\n\ndef cif28(d):\n    ajf = AalenJohansenFitter(calculate_variance=False, seed=20261120)\n    ajf.fit(d[DESIGN_DURATION], d[\"event_status\"], event_of_interest=1)\n    cd = ajf.cumulative_density_.iloc[:, 0]\n    return float(cd[cd.index <= 28].iloc[-1])\n\n\ndef counts(d):\n    return {\"n_exposed\": int(d[EXPOSURE].sum()),\n            \"deaths_exposed\": int(d.loc[d[EXPOSURE] == 1, DESIGN_EVENT].sum()),\n            \"n_unexposed\": int((1 - d[EXPOSURE]).sum()),\n            \"deaths_unexposed\": int(d.loc[d[EXPOSURE] == 0, DESIGN_EVENT].sum())}\n\n\ndef main():\n    m = read_parquet(\"matched_cohorts.parquet\")\n    m[\"fg_time\"] = np.where(m.event_status == 2, 28.0, m[DESIGN_DURATION])\n    m[\"fg_event\"] = (m.event_status == 1).astype(int)\n    n = int(m.imputation.value_counts().iloc[0])\n    cb, cv, fb, fv, c1, c0 = [], [], [], [], [], []\n    for _, d in m.groupby(\"imputation\"):\n        b, v, _ = cox_exposure(d, DESIGN_DURATION, DESIGN_EVENT, None, cluster=\"pair_id\")\n        cb.append(b); cv.append(v)\n        b, v, _ = cox_exposure(d, \"fg_time\", \"fg_event\", None, cluster=\"pair_id\")\n        fb.append(b); fv.append(v)\n        c1.append(cif28(d[d[EXPOSURE] == 1])); c0.append(cif28(d[d[EXPOSURE] == 0]))\n    d1 = m[m.imputation == 1]\n    rows = [hr_row(\"Design outcome: in-hospital death censored at discharge, PSM Cox\", rubin(cb, cv, n),\n                   population=\"PS-matched cohort\", outcome=\"28-day in-hospital mortality (design-specified)\",\n                   comparison=\"pravastatin vs no pravastatin\", note=\"cause-specific\", **counts(d1)),\n            hr_row(\"Design outcome: Fine-Gray (discharge alive competing), PSM\", rubin(fb, fv, n),\n                   population=\"PS-matched cohort\", outcome=\"28-day in-hospital mortality (subdistribution)\",\n                   comparison=\"pravastatin vs no pravastatin\",\n                   note=f\"CIF28 {np.mean(c1):.3f} vs {np.mean(c0):.3f}\", **counts(d1))]\n    rows[1][\"effect_measure\"] = \"sHR\"\n    out = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n    write_csv(out, \"design_outcome_results.csv\")\n    for r in out.itertuples():\n        log(\"a26\", f\"{r.analysis}: {r.effect_measure} {r.estimate:.3f} ({r.ci_low:.3f}-{r.ci_high:.3f}); {r.note}\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n", "outputs": [{"name": "design_outcome_results.csv", "kind": "csv", "exists": true, "bytes": 718, "rows": 2, "columns": [{"name": "analysis", "type": ""}, {"name": "effect_measure", "type": ""}, {"name": "estimate", "type": ""}, {"name": "ci_low", "type": ""}, {"name": "ci_high", "type": ""}, {"name": "p_value", "type": ""}, {"name": "status", "type": ""}, {"name": "population", "type": ""}, {"name": "outcome", "type": ""}, {"name": "comparison", "type": ""}, {"name": "note", "type": ""}, {"name": "n_exposed", "type": ""}, {"name": "deaths_exposed", "type": ""}, {"name": "n_unexposed", "type": ""}, {"name": "deaths_unexposed", "type": ""}]}]}, {"step": 27, "file": "a27_table2.py", "code": "\"\"\"\nAnalysis step 27. Publication-style results table with E-value\n\nInput     : primary_cox_results.csv, multivariable_cox_results.csv, secondary_outcome_results.csv,\n            sensitivity_confounding_results.csv, sensitivity_immortal_time_results.csv,\n            design_outcome_results.csv, subgroup_results.csv\nOperation : Stack all estimates into Table 2 and add the E-value for the primary HR and its CI\n            limit closest to 1 (RR = (1-0.5^sqrt(HR))/(1-0.5^sqrt(1/HR))). not_estimable rows keep\n            their status; no values are invented.\nOutput    : table2_mortality_associations.csv\n\"\"\"\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\nfrom common import log, read_csv, write_csv\n\nCOLUMNS = [\"section\", \"analysis\", \"population\", \"outcome\", \"comparison\", \"n_exposed\", \"deaths_exposed\",\n           \"n_unexposed\", \"deaths_unexposed\", \"effect_measure\", \"estimate\", \"ci_low\", \"ci_high\",\n           \"p_value\", \"status\", \"note\"]\n\n\ndef hr_to_rr(hr):\n    return (1 - 0.5 ** np.sqrt(hr)) / (1 - 0.5 ** np.sqrt(1 / hr))\n\n\ndef e_value(rr):\n    rr = 1 / rr if rr < 1 else rr\n    return rr + np.sqrt(rr * (rr - 1))\n\n\ndef main():\n    prim = read_csv(\"primary_cox_results.csv\").assign(section=\"Primary (PSM)\")\n    mv = read_csv(\"multivariable_cox_results.csv\").assign(section=\"Multivariable Cox (full cohort)\", note=\"\")\n    sec = read_csv(\"secondary_outcome_results.csv\").assign(section=\"Secondary outcomes (PSM)\")\n    sc = read_csv(\"sensitivity_confounding_results.csv\").assign(section=\"Sensitivity: confounding control\")\n    si = read_csv(\"sensitivity_immortal_time_results.csv\").assign(section=\"Sensitivity: immortal time\")\n    do = read_csv(\"design_outcome_results.csv\").assign(section=\"Design-specified outcome\")\n    sub = read_csv(\"subgroup_results.csv\")\n    sub = sub.assign(section=\"Subgroups (PSM)\", analysis=\"Subgroup: \" + sub.subgroup + \" = \" + sub.level,\n                     population=\"PS-matched, \" + sub.subgroup + \" = \" + sub.level,\n                     outcome=\"28-day all-cause mortality\", comparison=\"pravastatin vs no pravastatin\",\n                     note=sub.p_interaction.map(lambda p: f\"p for interaction {p:.3g}\"))\n    p = prim.iloc[0]\n    limit = 1.0 if p.ci_low <= 1 <= p.ci_high else (p.ci_high if p.estimate < 1 else p.ci_low)\n    ev = pd.DataFrame([{\"section\": \"Primary (PSM)\", \"analysis\": \"E-value for primary HR\",\n                        \"population\": \"PS-matched cohort\", \"outcome\": \"28-day all-cause mortality\",\n                        \"comparison\": \"pravastatin vs no pravastatin\", \"effect_measure\": \"E-value\",\n                        \"estimate\": e_value(hr_to_rr(p.estimate)), \"status\": \"estimated\",\n                        \"note\": f\"E-value for CI limit closest to 1: \"\n                                f\"{1.0 if limit == 1.0 else e_value(hr_to_rr(limit)):.2f}\"}])\n    out = pd.concat([prim, ev, mv, sec, sc, si, do, sub], ignore_index=True).reindex(columns=COLUMNS)\n    write_csv(out, \"table2_mortality_associations.csv\")\n    log(\"a27\", f\"Table 2 rows={len(out)}; primary HR {p.estimate:.3f} ({p.ci_low:.3f}-{p.ci_high:.3f}); \"\n               f\"E-value {ev.estimate.iloc[0]:.2f} ({ev.note.iloc[0]})\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n", "outputs": [{"name": "table2_mortality_associations.csv", "kind": "csv", "exists": true, "bytes": 10838, "rows": 39, "columns": [{"name": "section", "type": ""}, {"name": "analysis", "type": ""}, {"name": "population", "type": ""}, {"name": "outcome", "type": ""}, {"name": "comparison", "type": ""}, {"name": "n_exposed", "type": ""}, {"name": "deaths_exposed", "type": ""}, {"name": "n_unexposed", "type": ""}, {"name": "deaths_unexposed", "type": ""}, {"name": "effect_measure", "type": ""}, {"name": "estimate", "type": ""}, {"name": "ci_low", "type": ""}, {"name": "ci_high", "type": ""}, {"name": "p_value", "type": ""}, {"name": "status", "type": ""}, {"name": "note", "type": ""}]}]}, {"step": 28, "file": "a28_package_results.py", "code": "\"\"\"\nAnalysis step 28. Final standardized result packaging\n\nInput     : protocol_concordance.csv, cohort_outcome_counts.csv, missingness_summary.csv,\n            table1_baseline_characteristics.csv, propensity_overlap.csv, matched_balance.csv,\n            iptw_diagnostics.csv, weighted_balance.csv, km_survival_estimates.csv,\n            proportional_hazards_test.csv, table2_mortality_associations.csv, subgroup_results.csv\nOperation : One Excel sheet per input (xlsxwriter); matched-cohort Kaplan-Meier figure and a\n            forest plot of primary, multivariable, sensitivity and subgroup HRs (PNG).\nOutput    : pravastatin_28d_mortality_results.xlsx, km_matched.png, forest_plot.png\n\"\"\"\nimport matplotlib\n\nmatplotlib.use(\"Agg\")\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\nfrom common import log, path, read_csv\n\nSHEETS = {\n    \"protocol_concordance\": \"protocol_concordance.csv\",\n    \"cohort_counts\": \"cohort_outcome_counts.csv\",\n    \"missingness\": \"missingness_summary.csv\",\n    \"table1\": \"table1_baseline_characteristics.csv\",\n    \"ps_overlap\": \"propensity_overlap.csv\",\n    \"matched_balance\": \"matched_balance.csv\",\n    \"weight_diagnostics\": \"iptw_diagnostics.csv\",\n    \"weighted_balance\": \"weighted_balance.csv\",\n    \"km_survival\": \"km_survival_estimates.csv\",\n    \"ph_test\": \"proportional_hazards_test.csv\",\n    \"table2\": \"table2_mortality_associations.csv\",\n    \"subgroups\": \"subgroup_results.csv\",\n}\n\n\ndef km_figure():\n    s = read_csv(\"km_survival_estimates.csv\")\n    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(6, 4.2))\n    for g, color, label in ((\"pravastatin\", \"#1f6f8b\", \"Pravastatin\"),\n                            (\"no_pravastatin\", \"#c0504d\", \"No pravastatin (matched)\")):\n        d = s[s.group == g]\n        ax.step(d.day, d.survival_matched, where=\"post\", color=color, label=label)\n        ax.fill_between(d.day, d.survival_matched_min_over_imp, d.survival_matched_max_over_imp,\n                        step=\"post\", color=color, alpha=0.15, linewidth=0)\n    p = s.matched_logrank_p_median.iloc[0]\n    ax.text(1, 0.08, f\"log-rank p = {p:.3g} (median of 20 imputations)\", fontsize=8)\n    ax.set_xlabel(\"Days from ICU admission\")\n    ax.set_ylabel(\"28-day survival (all-cause)\")\n    ax.set_xlim(0, 28)\n    ax.set_ylim(0, 1)\n    ax.legend(frameon=False, loc=\"lower left\", bbox_to_anchor=(0, 0.12))\n    ax.set_title(\"Kaplan-Meier, 1:1 PS-matched cohort\", fontsize=10)\n    fig.tight_layout()\n    fig.savefig(path(\"km_matched.png\"), dpi=150)\n    plt.close(fig)\n\n\ndef forest_figure():\n    t2 = read_csv(\"table2_mortality_associations.csv\")\n    keep = t2[t2.effect_measure.isin([\"HR\", \"sHR\"])].copy().iloc[::-1].reset_index(drop=True)\n    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(8.5, 0.3 * len(keep) + 1))\n    y = np.arange(len(keep))\n    est = keep.estimate.to_numpy()\n    ok = ~np.isnan(est)\n    ax.errorbar(est[ok], y[ok], xerr=[est[ok] - keep.ci_low[ok], keep.ci_high[ok] - est[ok]],\n                fmt=\"s\", color=\"#1f3b57\", ecolor=\"#7a8a99\", capsize=2, markersize=4)\n    for yi in y[~ok]:\n        ax.text(1, yi, \"not estimable\", va=\"center\", ha=\"center\", fontsize=7, color=\"#888\")\n    ax.axvline(1, color=\"#999\", linestyle=\"--\", linewidth=0.8)\n    ax.set_yticks(y)\n    ax.set_yticklabels(keep.analysis, fontsize=7)\n    ax.set_xscale(\"log\")\n    ax.set_xlabel(\"Hazard ratio (log scale), pravastatin vs no pravastatin\")\n    fig.tight_layout()\n    fig.savefig(path(\"forest_plot.png\"), dpi=150)\n    plt.close(fig)\n\n\ndef main():\n    xlsx = path(\"pravastatin_28d_mortality_results.xlsx\")\n    with pd.ExcelWriter(xlsx, engine=\"xlsxwriter\") as w:\n        for sheet, f in SHEETS.items():\n            read_csv(f).to_excel(w, sheet_name=sheet, index=False)\n    km_figure()\n    forest_figure()\n    log(\"a28\", f\"wrote {xlsx.name}, km_matched.png, forest_plot.png\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n", "outputs": [{"name": "pravastatin_28d_mortality_results.xlsx", "kind": "xlsx", "exists": true, "bytes": 59236, "sheets": ["protocol_concordance", "cohort_counts", "missingness", "table1", "ps_overlap", "matched_balance", "weight_diagnostics", "weighted_balance", "km_survival", "ph_test", "table2", "subgroups"], "sheetSources": {"protocol_concordance": "protocol_concordance.csv", "cohort_counts": "cohort_outcome_counts.csv", "missingness": "missingness_summary.csv", "table1": "table1_baseline_characteristics.csv", "ps_overlap": "propensity_overlap.csv", "matched_balance": "matched_balance.csv", "weight_diagnostics": "iptw_diagnostics.csv", "weighted_balance": "weighted_balance.csv", "km_survival": "km_survival_estimates.csv", "ph_test": "proportional_hazards_test.csv", "table2": "table2_mortality_associations.csv", "subgroups": "subgroup_results.csv"}}, {"name": "km_matched.png", "kind": "png", "exists": true, "bytes": 40736}, {"name": "forest_plot.png", "kind": "png", "exists": true, "bytes": 147981}]}]};
